hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15601","502 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti told us: My father told us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya told us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah told us: Ismail ibn Ayyash told us: from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Azhar ibn Abdullah, from Ismah ibn Qays, a companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to seek refuge in his prayer from the trial of the West."
"15602","Ujayr ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz. 503 - Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah told us: from Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari who said: Ujayr ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz lived in Makkah, he narrated a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Muhammad ibn Ismail did not mention the hadith."
"15603","Arib Abu Abdullah al-Mulayki. 504 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Aqal al-Harrani told us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli told us: Said ibn Sinan told us: from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Arib al-Mulayki, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that this verse was revealed: Those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly, that it was revealed about spending on horses."
"15604","505 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Aqal told us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli told us: Said ibn Sinan told us: from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Arib, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Horses have good and arrows tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their people are aided in them, and the spender on them is like one stretching his hands in charity, and their urine and dung will be for their people with Allah on the Day of Resurrection like the musk of Paradise."
"15605","506 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi told us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur told us: from Said ibn Sinan, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Arib al-Mulayki, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying: And others besides them whom you do not know, Allah knows them, that they are the jinn. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No house containing a noble horse is ruined by confusion."
"15606","Ufayr ibn Abi Ufayr. 507 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati told us: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi told us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Mulayki told us: from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, from his father, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said to a man from the Arabs called Ufayr ibn Abi Ufayr: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak about affection? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Affection is inherited, and hatred is inherited."
"15607","508 - Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar told us: Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi told us: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah Abu al-Mundhir al-Warraq told us: from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq met a man from the Arabs called Ufayr ibn Abi Ufayr, and Abu Bakr said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about affection? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Affection is inherited, and enmity is inherited."
"15608","The uncle of Kharijah ibn al-Salt, it is said his name is Ilaqah ibn Suhar. 509 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Abu Nuaym told us: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah told us: from al-Shabi, from Kharijah ibn al-Salt, that an uncle of his came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and became Muslim, and when he returned he passed by a mad Bedouin bound in iron, and some of them said to him: Do you have anything with which to treat him, for your companion has come with good? He said: Yes. He said: So I treated him with the Mother of the Book for three days, twice each day, and he recovered, and they gave me one hundred sheep, but I did not take them until I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Did you say anything besides this? I said: No. He said: Eat them, in the name of Allah; by my life, if one eats by a false charm, you have eaten by a true charm."
"15609","Those named Aqil. Aqil ibn Abi Talib - kunya Abu Yazid - ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim. He was present at the conquest of Khaybar, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted him from Khaybar, mentioned in al-Maghazi. From the reports of Aqil. 510 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Abu Nuaym told us: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami told us: from Abu Ishaq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aqil ibn Abi Talib: O Abu Yazid, I love you with two loves: for your kinship to me, and a love for what I knew of my uncle's love for you."
"15610","What Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated. 511 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna told us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dharra told us, (Ha). And Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani told us: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba told us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad told us, (Ha). And Abdan ibn Ahmad told us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr told us, (Ha). And Ibrahim ibn Mattuwayh al-Ansari told us: Abu Kurayb told us, they said: Yunus ibn Bukayr told us: Talhah ibn Yahya told us: from Musa ibn Talhah: Aqil ibn Abi Talib told me, he said: Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said: Your nephew harms us in our club and in our gathering, so forbid him from harming us. So he said to me: O Aqil, go to Muhammad. So I went to him and brought him out of a kibs - Talhah said: a small house - and he came in the midday heat, seeking shade to walk in from the intense heat of the sun-baked ground. So we came to them, and Abu Talib said: Your cousins claim you harm them in their club and gathering, so desist from that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his gaze to the sky and said: Do you see this sun? They said: Yes. He said: I am no more able to leave that than you are able to kindle a flame from it. Abu Talib said: Our nephew has never lied to us, so go back."
"15611","512 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud told us: Asad ibn Musa told us, (Ha). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: Abu Umar al-Darir told us, they said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi told us: from al-Hasan, that Aqil ibn Abi Talib married a woman and it was said to him: With harmony and sons. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you marries, let it be said to him: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you."
"15612","513 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri: Abu Said al-Basri told me that he heard al-Hasan. Abd al-Razzaq said, and Ibn Jurayj told me, from a man, from al-Hasan, mentioning from Aqil ibn Abi Talib, that he married a woman from Banu Jusham and it was said to him: With harmony and sons. He said: Do not say that, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, and ordered us to say: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you."
"15613","514 - Yusuf al-Qadi told us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir told us: Yazid ibn Zuray told us: Yunus told us: from al-Hasan, that Aqil ibn Abi Talib married a woman from Banu Jusham ibn Sad, and the people came to him and began congratulating him, saying: With harmony and sons. He said: Do not say that. They said: How should we say, O Abu Yazid? He said: Say: May Allah bless for you, and may Allah bless upon you; we were ordered with that."
"15614","515 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: My father told us: Zuhayr told us: al-Husayn ibn Dinar told us: from al-Hasan, who said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib came to us and married a woman from Banu Jusham, then he came out and they said: With harmony and sons. He said: Do not say this, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to say With harmony and sons, and ordered us to say: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you."
"15615","516 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi told us: Abd al-Salam ibn Asim told us: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib told us: from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Hasan, who said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib came to us and entered, and it was said: With harmony and sons. He said: Say what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless among you and bless for you."
"15616","517 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari told us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri told us: Sufyan told us: from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, who said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib came to Basrah and married a woman, and they said to her: With harmony and sons. He said: Do not say that, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, and ordered us to say: May Allah bless for you and bless upon you."
"15617","518 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr told us: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali told us: Abu Qutaybah told us: al-Rabi ibn Subayh told us: from al-Hasan, who said: Aqil ibn Abi Talib came, and he mentioned similar to it."
"15618","Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud al-Ansari, Aqabi, and the people of Kufah say: Badri, while the people of Basrah did not mention him among those who witnessed Badr. Reports of Abu Masud and his death. 519 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: My father told me: Ibn Lahiah told us: from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: Among the names of those who witnessed al-Aqabah to pledge to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj: Uqbah ibn Amr ibn Thalabah ibn Yusayr ibn Asiysah, kunya Abu Masud."
"15619","520 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi told us: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham told us: Ziyad ibn Abdullah told us: from Ibn Ishaq: Among the names of those who witnessed al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from al-Khazraj: Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr ibn Thalabah ibn Yusayr ibn Asiysah ibn Hadarah ibn Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj."
"15620","521 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Arim Abu al-Numan told us: Hammad ibn Zayd told us: from Mujalid, from al-Shabi who said: When Ali went out to Siffin he left Abu Masud in charge over Kufah, and there were men from the people of Kufah who had hidden from Ali, and when he left they appeared, and people would come to Abu Masud saying: By Allah, Allah has destroyed His enemies and granted the believers victory. So Abu Masud would say: By Allah, I do not count it a victory nor well-being that one of the two parties prevails over the other. They said: Then what? He said: There will be peace between the people. When Ali returned, they mentioned that to him, and Ali said: Keep away from our office. He said: And what is that? He said: We found you do not restrain a restraint. He said: As for me, there remains of my intellect what I know that the end is evil."
"15621","What Abu Masud narrated. Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Masud. 522 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: Sulayman ibn Harb told us: Shubah told us. Abu Muslim said: And Amr ibn Marzuq told us: Shubah told us: from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Masud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man spends on his family, reckoning it, it is charity for him. I said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15622","523 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan told us: My father told us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman told us: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj told me: from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. Thus Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it."
"15623","Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abu Masud. 524 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam told us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi told us, (Ha). And Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi told us: Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us: from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud who said: There was among us a man called Abu Shuayb, and he had a butcher slave. He said to his slave: Prepare food for me, perhaps I will invite the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the fifth of five, and a man followed him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: You invited me as the fifth of five, and this one has followed us; if you permit, else he will return. He said: Rather we permit him."
"15624","525 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim told us, (Ha). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: Sulayman ibn Harb and Amr ibn Marzuq told us, they said: Shubah told us: from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud who said: A man prepared food, called Abu Shuayb, and invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him five. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought his permission regarding the sixth."
"15625","526 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis told us: al-Abbas ibn Talib told us: Abu Awanah told us: from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man from the Ansar, kunya Abu Shuayb, said to his slave: Woe to you, I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so prepare food sufficient for five. So he prepared it, and he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him, and a man who was not invited followed them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one has followed us, so will you permit him? He said: Yes."
"15626","527 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid told us: My father told us: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah told us: from Sulayman al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Uqbah ibn Amr who said: Abu Shuayb had a butcher slave, and when he saw what was upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions of hardship, he ordered his slave to bring meat sufficient for five. So he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come as the fifth of five. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came as the fifth of five, and a sixth man followed them. When he reached the door of Abu Shuayb, he said: You sent to five, and this one has followed us; if you permit him he will enter, else he will return. He said: No, rather I have permitted him, let him eat."
"15627","528 - Bakr ibn Sahl told us: Ahmad ibn Shukayb al-Kufi told us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl told us: from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr who said: A man from the Ansar called Abu Shuayb had a butcher slave, and he said to his slave: I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps I will invite him as the fifth of five. So he prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and invited him as the fifth of five, and a man followed them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has followed us; if you wish, permit him."
"15628","529 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad told us: Asim ibn Ali told us: Ishaq al-Azraq told us: from Sufyan and Sharik, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud, that a man had a butcher slave, and he said to his slave: Prepare food for us sufficient for five or six; perhaps I will invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the fifth of five. So he invited them and a man followed them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You invited me as the fifth of five, and this one has followed us; if you wish, permit him, and if you wish, leave him. He said: Rather I permit him."
"15629","530 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah told us: Jarir told us: from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud who said: A man from the Ansar called Abu Shuayb had a butcher slave, and he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and recognized hunger in his face. He said to his slave: Woe to you, prepare food for me, for I want to invite the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the fifth of five. So he prepared, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him as the fifth of five, and a man followed them. When he reached the door, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one has followed us; if you wish, permit him, and if you wish, he returns. He said: No, rather I permit him, O Messenger of Allah."
"15630","531 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us: Abu Muawiyah told us: from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Masud who said: A man from the Ansar called Abu Shuayb said to a butcher slave of his: Prepare food for me sufficient for five, for I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he prepared food for him, then he sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions who were with him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, a man who had not been with them when he invited them followed them. When they reached the door, he said to the owner of the house: A man has followed me and was not present when you invited us; if you permit him, he will enter. He said: We have permitted him, let him enter."
"15631","532 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil told us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr told us: My father told us: from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Masud, from a man from the Ansar, kunya Abu Shuayb, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and recognized hunger in his face, so I met a butcher slave of mine and ordered him to prepare food for five men, then I invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he came as the fifth of five, and a man followed them. When he reached the door, he said: This one has followed us; if you wish, permit him, else he will return. So I permitted him."
"15632","Chapter. 533 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah told us: Abu Usamah told us: from Zaidah, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Uqbah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order charity, so a man would go and carry heavily and come with a mudd, though today some of them have one hundred thousand. Shaqiq said: I saw that he was alluding to himself."
"15633","534 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah told us, they said: Abu Usamah told us: from Zaidah, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Uqbah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order charity, so a man would go and carry heavily and come with a mudd, though today some of them have one hundred thousand. Shaqiq said: I saw that he was alluding to himself."
"15634","535 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi told us: Amr ibn Marzuq told us: Shubah told us: from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud who said: We would carry loads, and one of us would come with little charity, and a man would come with half a sa, and some hypocrites would mock us, so revealed: Those who criticize the voluntary givers among the believers concerning charities, the verse."
"15635","536 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi told us: My uncle Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman told us: Husayn ibn Ali told us: from Zaidah, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud who said: We would carry loads for charity, and one of us would come with a sa, and some hypocrites would mock them, so revealed: Those who criticize the voluntary givers among the believers concerning charities."
"15636","537 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq told us: Yahya al-Himmani told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us: from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man from those before you was reckoned, and nothing of good was found for him except that he dealt with people, and he was wealthy and would order his slave to overlook the insolvent. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: We are more entitled than he, so overlook him. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said in his hadith: We are more entitled than he to overlook him, so He overlooked him."
"15637","Mughirah ibn Miqsam, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud. 538 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Abu Nuaym told us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb told us: from Mughirah, from Shaqiq, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Men from my companions will be raised to me until when I see them they will be snatched away from me. So I will say: My companions. Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"15638","al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud. 539 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari told us: Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan told us: Uthman ibn Umar told us: Shubah told us: from al-Hakam, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud: That a man from the Ansar, kunya Abu Shuayb, prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Come to me with five. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you permit the sixth?"
"15639","Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Abu Wail, from Abu Masud. 540 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuwayh al-Asbahani told us: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi told us: al-Fadl ibn Musa told us: from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Mansur, from Shaqiq, from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order charity, and none of us would find anything to give in charity until he went to the market and carried on his back, then came with the charity and gave it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I know today a man with one hundred thousand who did not have a dirham that day."
"15640","Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abu Masud. 541 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami told us: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi told us: Sharik told us: from Asim, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Alqamah, from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites them in a night, they suffice him: the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah."
"15641","542 - Musa ibn Harun told us: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari told us: Hammad ibn Salamah told us: from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Alqamah ibn Qays, that Abu Masud al-Badri said: Whoever recites the ending of Surat al-Baqarah, it suffices him for a night's recitation. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the seals of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne."
"15642","543 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil told us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath told us: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Alqamah, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah: whoever recites them in a night, they suffice him."
"15643","544 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad told us: Asim ibn Ali told us: Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah told us: from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a man recites two verses from the end of al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him: The Messenger believes in what was revealed to him from his Lord."
"15644","545 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri told us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi told us: Amr ibn Uthman told us: Abu Muslim told us: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites these two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him: The Messenger believes in what was revealed to him from his Lord, to the end of the surah. Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid said: I came to Abu Masud al-Ansari while he was circumambulating, and I asked about him, and he told me this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15645","546 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad told us: Asim ibn Ali told us: Qays ibn al-Rabi and Abu Marwan Zakariyya ibn Abi Yahya al-Ghassani told us: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Alqamah, from Abu Masud who said: I met Abu Masud while he was circumambulating the House, and I said: A hadith Alqamah told me from you. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah: whoever recites them in a night, they suffice him: The Messenger believes in what was revealed to him from his Lord."
"15646","547 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us: Abdullah ibn Numayr told us: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"15647","548 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: My father told us: Zuhayr told us: Sulayman told us: from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid - I think from Abu Masud - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah: whoever recites them in a night, they suffice him."
"15648","549 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Abu Muawiyah told us: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah: whoever recites them in a night, they suffice him. And he did not mention Alqamah."
"15649","550 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: Sulayman ibn Harb told us: Shubah told us: from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him. And al-Amash said: from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, similar to it."
"15650","551 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told us: Muawiyah ibn Amr told us: Zaidah told us: from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Uqbah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites in a night the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah, they suffice him."
"15651","552 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And he added: Abd al-Rahman said: Alqamah told me it, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I met Abu Masud in circumambulation and asked him about it, and he told me it while circumambulating."
"15652","553 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani told us: My father told us: Zuhayr told us: Mansur told us: from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid who said: I came to Abu Masud and said: Abu Masud, it reached me from you about the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah: whoever recites them in a night, they suffice him."
"15653","554 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari told us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah told us: Jarir told us: from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"15654","Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 555 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari told us: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I do not attend prayer because so-and-so lengthens for us. I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angrier in an exhortation than he was that day, then he said: Whoever leads people, let him lighten for them, for behind him are the weak, the small, the old, and the needy."
"15655","556 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi told us: Amr ibn Marzuq told us: Shubah told us: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I pray behind so-and-so, and he lengthens the prayer, so perhaps I stay back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry with an anger I never saw him angry with in an exhortation, and said: Some of you are repellers; whoever leads people, let him lighten the prayer for them, for among them are the weak, the old, and the needy."
"15656","557 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told us: Muawiyah ibn Amr told us: Zaidah told us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid told us: from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I stay back from Fajr prayer because of so-and-so who lengthens for us. I never saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ever angrier in an exhortation than that day, and he said: O people, some of you are repellers; whichever of you prays for people, let him be brief, for among them are the weak, the old, and the needy."
"15657","558 - Bishr ibn Musa told us: al-Humaydi told us: Sufyan told us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid told us, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim saying: I heard Abu Masud saying: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I stay behind from morning prayer. And he mentioned the hadith."
"15658","559 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis told us: Ali ibn Mabad told us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr told us: from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I stay behind from Fajr prayer because of what so-and-so lengthens for us in recitation. I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in an exhortation he exhorted, angrier than that day, then he said: Whoever prays with people, let him lighten the prayer for them, for among them are the small, the old, the weak, and the needy."
"15659","560 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatawani told us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath told us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim told us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid told us: from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Qays al-Ansari who said: A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I stay back from morning prayer because of so-and-so, from what he lengthens for us. I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever angrier in an exhortation than that day, and he said: O people, some of you are repellers; whichever of you prays with people, let him be brief, for among them are the weak, the old, and the needy."
"15660","561 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna told us: Musaddad told us: Yahya ibn Said told us: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I stay back from prayer because of so-and-so, from what he lengthens for us. I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angrier in an exhortation than that day, and he said: O people, some of you are repellers; whichever of you prays with people, let him be brief, for among them are the old, the weak, and the needy."
"15661","562 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15662","563 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Khallad al-Saffar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15663","Chapter 564 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Harshness, hard-heartedness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen, the dwellers of wool tents, at the roots of camels' tails, from Rabiah and Mudar."
"15664","565 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed toward Yemen and said: Faith is here, and harshness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabiah and Mudar."
"15665","566 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed toward Yemen and said: Faith is here, faith is here; indeed harshness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabiah and Mudar."
"15666","567 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is here, and he pointed with his hand toward Yemen; and harshness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen at the roots of camels' tails, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabiah and Mudar."
"15667","568 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris and Jarir narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed toward Yemen and said: Faith is here; harshness and thickness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen at the roots of camels' tails, where the horn of Satan rises, among Rabiah and Mudar."
"15668","569 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Khallad al-Saffar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15669","Chapter 570 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, who said: I heard Qays say: I heard Abu Masud say: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, so people said: It eclipsed because of Ibrahim's death. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are two signs among Allah's signs; they do not eclipse for anyone's death nor for his life, so when you see that, hasten to the remembrance of Allah and to prayer."
"15670","571 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
"15671","572 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are two signs among Allah's signs, and they do not eclipse for anyone's death, so when you see them, pray until they clear."
"15672","573 - Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), coinciding with the death of Ibrahim, and he said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for anyone's death nor for his life, but when you see them, pray."
"15673","574 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so people said: The sun only eclipsed because of the death of Ibrahim, peace be upon him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for anyone's death nor for his life, but they are two signs among Allah's signs, so when you see them, pray."
"15674","575 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir and Waki narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for any person's death, but they are two signs among Allah's signs, so when you see them, stand for prayer."
"15675","576 - Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Khuzai narrated to us. (Ha) al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Ruasi narrated to us. (Ha) Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us; they said: Hammad ibn Said al-Barra narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead ewe and said: It would not have harmed its owners had they benefited from its hide."
"15676","Bayan ibn Bishr from Qays from Abu Masud. 577 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Yemen and said: Faith is Yemeni, and harshness and thickness of hearts are at camels' tails among the loud-voiced herdsmen, among Rabiah and Mudar, where the two horns of Satan rise."
"15677","Abu Mamar Abdullah ibn Sakhbarah from Abu Masud. 578 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer suffices in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration."
"15678","579 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us; both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of any one - or he said: of a man - who does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration does not suffice."
"15679","580 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umayrah, from Abu Mamar, from Uqbah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No prayer is to be hoped for in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration."
"15680","581 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer suffices in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration - or he said: when he bows and when he prostrates - Abu Awanah doubted."
"15681","582 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer is to be hoped for in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration. Sufyan said: Thus al-Amash said, do not hope for: it does not suffice."
"15682","583 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah and Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer suffices in which a man does not straighten his backbone in bowing and prostration."
"15683","584 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khali al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Salamah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ruasi, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Uqbah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The prayer of a man who does not straighten his backbone for bowing and prostration is not accepted."
"15684","585 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ubayd, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15685","Chapter 586 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15686","587 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us; both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our shoulders in prayer and say: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15687","588 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our shoulders in prayer and say: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15688","589 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Dawud al-Tai, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders and say: Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15689","590 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15690","Chapter 591 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Let those of understanding and reason be closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"15691","592 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us; both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Let those of understanding and reason be closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"15692","593 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah, from Abu Mamar, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Let those of understanding and reason be closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"15693","594 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Let those of understanding and reason be closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"15694","595 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Dawud al-Tai, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Let those of understanding and reason be closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"15695","596 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15696","597 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let those who learn from me be closest to me - meaning in prayer."
"15697","598 - Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Mamar, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: Straighten the shoulders, establish the rows, and do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"15698","599 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ishaq al-Taymi narrated to us, who said: I heard Ubayd ibn Hisn, who reported it from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Masud, in a raised report, who said: Whoever recites the last two verses of al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"15699","Aws ibn Damaj from Abu Masud. 600 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja al-Zubaydi, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most entitled of people to lead them in prayer is the most reciting of Allah's Book; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. No man is to be led in prayer in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15700","601 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting lead the people in prayer; if they are equal in recitation, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in knowledge, then the oldest in age. No man is to be led in prayer in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15701","602 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. No man is to be led in prayer in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission. Zaidah said: I said to Sulayman: Is his honored seat the head of his bedding? He said: Yes."
"15702","603 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, who said: We memorized it from al-Amash, who said: I heard Ismail ibn Raja narrate from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the oldest in age. No one is led in prayer in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat except with his permission."
"15703","604 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the oldest in age. No man is to lead another in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15704","605 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the most reciting of the Quran lead you; if your recitation is the same, then the earliest in emigration; if your emigration is the same, then the oldest in age. No man leads another in his domain nor among his family, and do not sit apart from his honored seat except with his permission."
"15705","606 - al-Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting lead the people; if the recitation is the same, then the earliest in emigration; if the emigration is the same, then the most understanding in jurisprudence; if the understanding is the same, then the oldest in age. No man is to be led in prayer in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15706","607 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik and Mandal ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in it, then the earliest in Islam. Do not lead a man in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15707","608 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book and the earliest in emigration lead the people; if they are equal, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in it, then the oldest in age. No man is led in prayer in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15708","609 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. No man is to lead another in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat except with his permission."
"15709","610 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khali narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Salamah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awsi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ruasi, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in knowledge of the Sunnah, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. Do not lead anyone in his authority, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15710","611 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the oldest in age. Do not lead anyone in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15711","612 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdallah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15712","613 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us. (Ha) Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us. (Ha) Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us; they said: Shubah, from Ismail ibn Raja, who said: I heard Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud al-Badri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if their recitation is the same, then the earliest in emigration; if their emigration is the same, then the oldest in age. No man is led in prayer among his family nor in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat except with his permission, unless he permits you. Shubah said: I said to him: What is his honored seat? He said: His bedding. And the wording is from Hajjaj's hadith."
"15713","614 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. No man is to be led in prayer in his domain, nor among his family, and no one sits on his honored seat unless he permits him."
"15714","615 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydallah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earliest in emigration lead the people; if their emigration is the same, then the oldest in age; if they are equal in age, then the most reciting."
"15715","616 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati and Ubayd al-Ijli said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, and Shubah, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. Do not lead a man of authority in his domain, and do not sit on his honored seat except with his permission."
"15716","617 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar al-Ansari narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earliest in emigration lead the people; if they are equal in emigration, then the most understanding in religion; if they are equal in understanding, then the most reciting of the Quran. No man is led in prayer in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat except with his permission."
"15717","618 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15718","619 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Dawud al-Qantari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the most reciting of Allah's Book lead you; if the recitation is the same, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if the Sunnah is the same, then the earliest in emigration; if the emigration is the same, then the oldest in age."
"15719","620 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti and Abdan ibn Ahmad said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of Allah's Book lead the people; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if they are equal in knowledge, then the earliest in emigration; if they are equal in emigration, then the oldest in age. No man leads another in his domain, and no one sits on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"15720","621 - Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather Abu Yazid, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the earliest in recitation lead you, and he mentioned something similar."
"15721","Abu Amr al-Shaybani from Abu Masud. 622 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of whoever does it."
"15722","623 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mount has perished, so carry me. He said: I find nothing to carry you on, but go to so-and-so, perhaps he will carry you. So he went to him and he carried him, then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer."
"15723","624 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mount has perished, so carry me. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have nothing, but go to so-and-so and ask him, perhaps he will carry you. So he went to him and he carried him, then he passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him that he had carried him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer."
"15724","625 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Carry me. He said: I find nothing to carry you on, but go to so-and-so, perhaps he will carry you. So he went to him and he carried him, and he mentioned that to him, and he said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer."
"15725","626 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (Ha) Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mount has perished, so carry me - meaning my journey was cut off, so carry me - and he said: I have nothing. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I will guide him to one who will carry him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer."
"15726","627 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated to us. (Ha) Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbui narrated to us; both said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Carry me. He said: I have nothing to carry you on, but go to so-and-so, for he has what will carry you. So he went to him and he carried him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good is like its doer."
"15727","628 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The one who guides to good is like its doer."
"15728","629 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahr al-Kufi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who guides to good is like its doer."
"15729","630 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good has the like of the reward of its doer."
"15730","631 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahr al-Kufi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who guides to good is like its doer."
"15731","632 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yunus al-Bakkari al-Shirazi narrated to us, al-Hurr ibn Malik narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mount has perished, so carry me. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I find nothing to carry you on, but go to so-and-so and he will carry you. So he went to him and he carried him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who guides to good is like its doer, or like its worker."
"15732","633 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbui narrated to us. (Ha) Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a bridled she-camel and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is in the path of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you in return are seven hundred she-camels on the Day of Resurrection, all bridled."
"15733","634 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: A man came with a bridled she-camel and said: This is in the path of Allah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you in return are seven hundred she-camels, all bridled."
"15734","635 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a bridled she-camel and said: O Messenger of Allah, in the path of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For you in return on the Day of Resurrection are seven hundred bridled she-camels."
"15735","636 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a bridled she-camel and said: This is in the path of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed for you in return are one hundred she-camels in Paradise."
"15736","637 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahr al-Kufi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"15737","638 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us; both said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"15738","639 - Hajib ibn Arkin al-Farghani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good deed is charity."
"15739","Masruq al-Ajda from Abu Masud, may Allah be pleased with him. 640 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the first prophethood is a man's saying: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15740","Ribi ibn Hirash from Abu Masud. Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Ribi. 641 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man died and it was said to him: What did you do? He said: I used to trade with people and be lenient in the marketplace, and grant respite to the insolvent. Then he died and entered Paradise. Then Abu Masud al-Badri said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15741","642 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, who said: Uqbah ibn Amr said to Hudhayfah: Will you not narrate to us what you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: With the Dajjal when he emerges are fire and water; as for what people see as fire, it is water, and as for what people see as water, it is fire. So whoever among you reaches that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is sweet cool water. Hudhayfah said: I heard him say: A man from those before you was visited by the angel to take his soul, and it was said to him: Did you do any good? He said: I do not know. It was said: Look. He said: I know nothing except that I used to trade with people in the world and be generous with them; I would grant respite to the insolvent and overlook the solvent, so Allah admitted him to Paradise. And I heard him say: A man was approached by death, and when he despaired of life he advised his family: When I die, gather much firewood for a year, then on a windy day scatter me in the sea. So they did, and Allah gathered him and said: Why did you do that? He said: Out of fear of You, so Allah forgave him. Uqbah said: And I heard him say that, and he was."
"15742","643 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, who said: Uqbah ibn Amr said to Hudhayfah: Will you not narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard him say: With the Dajjal when he emerges are water and fire; as for what people see as fire, it is cool water. So whoever among you reaches that, let him fall into what people see as fire, for it is sweet cool water. Then Uqbah ibn Amr said: And I heard him say that."
"15743","644 - Shuayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah and Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15744","Nuaym ibn Abi Hind from Ribi ibn Hirash. 645 - Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Salamah al-Awsi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us. (Ha) Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us. (Ha) al-Qasim ibn Furak al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman narrated to us, all of them from al-Ajlah, from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, from Ribi ibn Hirash, who said: I sat with Hudhayfah and Abu Masud al-Ansari, and one of them said to the other: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The other said: Rather you narrate and I will confirm you. So one of them narrated and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: Look into his deeds. He will say: My Lord, I did no good except that I had wealth and I dealt with people; whoever was solvent I made easy for him, and whoever was insolvent I granted him respite until ease. Then Allah the Exalted said: I am most entitled to make easy, so He forgave him. And he said: You spoke the truth; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and he had said to his family: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then face a violent wind with me and scatter me. So Allah gathered him on the Day of Resurrection and said: Why did you do that? He said: Out of fear of You, so He forgave him. He said: You spoke the truth; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that. And the wording is from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra's hadith."
"15745","646 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, from Ribi ibn Hirash, who said: Hudhayfah and Abu Masud gathered, and Hudhayfah said: I know best what is with the Dajjal; with him are a river of fire and a river of water, and what they see as fire is water, and what they see as water is fire. So whoever among you reaches that should drink from what he sees as fire, for he will find it water. Then Abu Masud said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"15746","Abu Malik al-Ashjai from Ribi. 647 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us. (Ha) al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai Said ibn Tariq, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, that a man from those before you commanded regarding his corpse when he died that it be burned, then ground, then lifted, and when there was a violent wind it be scattered in it. So he was gathered to his Lord, and He said: Woe to you, what carried you to this? He said: My Lord, no servant was bolder against You than I, nor more disobedient to You than I, yet I hoped to escape, so He forgave him. Then Abu Masud said: Thus I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15747","648 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us. (Ha) Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, who said: A man commanded his family when he died to burn him, then crush him, then scatter him on a windy tempestuous day. So they did, and he was gathered to his Lord, mighty and majestic, and He said: What carried you to what you did? He said: There was no servant of Yours, my Lord, more disobedient to You than I, yet I hoped to escape. Then He said: Overlook My servant, so He forgave him. Then Abu Masud said: Thus I heard it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15748","649 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai informed us, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, that a man was brought by his Lord, mighty and majestic, and He said: What did you do for Me in the world? He said: I did nothing for You worth a speck of good that I hope for, except that I was a man to whom You had given wealth with which I traded with people, and it was of my character to overlook; I would make easy for the solvent and grant respite to the insolvent. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Say: We are most entitled to that; overlook My servant, so He forgave him. Then Abu Masud said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"15749","650 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, brought a servant of His and said: What did you do? He says: I did nothing much of prayer or fasting by which I hope for You, except that You had given me abundance of wealth, so I dealt with people; I would make easy for the solvent and grant respite to the insolvent. Then He said: We are most entitled to that; overlook My servant, so Allah forgave him."
"15750","Mansur ibn al-Mutamir from Ribi ibn Hirash. 651 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Khalifah said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15751","652 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us. (Ha) Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us; both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15752","653 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, Ribi ibn Hirash narrated to me, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15753","654 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said Abu Umar al-Darir al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15754","655 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15755","656 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15756","657 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15757","658 - Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, from Abu Shaybah, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15758","659 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik and Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what was learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15759","660 - Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb and Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"15760","661 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people have learned from the words of the first prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"15761","662 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri. (Ha) Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: We woke fasting to complete thirty days in Ramadan, then two Bedouin men came and testified before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they had sighted the crescent yesterday evening, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them and they broke fast. And the wording is from Abu Hudhayfah's hadith."
"15762","663 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud, who said: People woke fasting to complete thirty days, then two men came and testified that they had seen the crescent yesterday, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the people and they broke fast. No one narrated in this hadith, from Ibn Uyaynah nor from anyone else, from Abu Masud, except Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani."
"15763","664 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels received the soul of a man before you and said to him: Did you ever do any good? He said: No, except that I used to give loans to people, and I would order my lads to grant respite to the solvent and overlook the insolvent. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Overlook."
"15764","Yusayer ibn Amr from Abu Masud. 665 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Qays ibn Yusayer ibn Amr, from his father, who said: I saw Abu Masud when Ali was killed, so I followed him and said: I adjure you by Allah, what did you hear from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tribulations? He said: We conceal nothing; upon you is fear of Allah and the community, and beware of division, for it is misguidance. Allah, mighty and majestic, would not gather the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon misguidance."
"15765","666 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, who said: I heard Yusayer ibn Amr, that Abu Masud al-Ansari, when Uthman was killed, secluded himself in his house, so I entered upon him and asked him about people's affairs, and he said: Upon you is the community, for Allah, mighty and majestic, has not gathered the nation of Muhammad upon misguidance; and be patient until a righteous one rests or rest is had from a wicked one."
"15766","667 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Arif al-Shaybani, from Yusayer ibn Amr, who said: Abu Masud al-Ansari set out in this direction, and I went out with him until when we were at al-Saylahayn he alighted and I alighted with him. When I saw him alone, I stood to him and said: O Abu Masud, there were among us three of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); as for Hudhayfah, he died, as for Abu Musa, he went to Syria, and you have taken this direction while there has occurred of tribulations what you see. He said to me: O Yusayer, I am advising you: cling to the community, for Allah would not gather the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon misguidance, until a righteous one rests or rest is had from a wicked one."
"15767","Salim al-Barrad from Abu Masud. 668 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, Salim al-Barrad narrated to me - and he was more trustworthy to me than myself - who said: Abu Masud al-Badri said to us: Shall I not pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So when he bowed he placed his palms on his knees, spread his fingers, and kept clear of his armpits until everything of him settled. Then he said Allah is Greatest, then prostrated and kept clear of his armpits until everything of him settled. Then he said Allah is Greatest and sat upright until everything of him settled. So he prayed with us four cycles thus, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray, or thus was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15768","669 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim al-Barrad, who said: Abu Masud al-Ansari said: Shall I not pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were with him? So he stood and said Allah is Greatest, then placed his palms on his knees, and he mentioned something similar."
"15769","670 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim Abu Abdallah, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: Shall I not pray with you as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? We said: Yes. So he stood and prayed; when he bowed he placed his palms on his knees, placed his fingers behind his knees, and kept his armpits clear until everything of him settled. Then he raised his head and stood until everything of him settled. Then he prostrated and kept his armpits clear until everything of him settled. Then he sat until everything of him settled. Then he prostrated and kept his armpits clear until everything of him settled. Then he did that for four cycles, then said: Thus he used to pray with us."
"15770","671 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abdallah, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: Shall I pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We said: Yes. So he stood and said Allah is Greatest, then bowed and placed his palms on his knees, placed his fingers below his knees, and kept his armpits clear until everything of him settled in its place. Then he raised until everything of him settled, then prostrated and placed his palms on the ground, kept between his armpits clear, and raised his head. Then when everything of him settled, he returned and did the like of that for four cycles, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray with us."
"15771","672 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas and Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim al-Barrad, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as the previous hadith."
"15772","673 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim al-Barrad, from Abu Masud, who said: Shall I not pray with you as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15773","674 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Abdallah al-Barrad, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray; when he bowed he straightened his back, so that if water were poured on his back it would settle."
"15774","Khalid ibn Sad from Abu Masud al-Ansari. 675 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us. (Ha) Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Wasiti narrated to us; they said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khalid ibn Sad, from Abu Masud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirsted around the Kabah and asked for drink, so he was brought the infused drink of the water service, and it was brought near to his mouth and he frowned. A man said: Is it unlawful? He said: No."
"15775","676 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan al-Marwazi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Samurah ibn Atiyyah, from Khalid ibn Sad, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No sacrifice with a slit-eared, pierced-eared, split-eared or torn-eared animal, and soundness of eye and ear."
"15776","677 - Abu Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Asbahani and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ala narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Khalid ibn Sad, from Abu Masud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The maternal aunt is a mother."
"15777","678 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdallah ibn Humran narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Khalid ibn Sad, from Abu Masud, who said: He used to forbid plundering at weddings."
"15778","Abu Abdallah al-Jadali from Abu Masud. 679 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdallah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr at the start of the night, its middle and its end."
"15779","680 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdallah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud al-Badri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr at the start of the night, its end and its middle."
"15780","681 - Ahmad ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Zufar, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdallah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr and Abu Musa al-Ashari, that they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes perform witr at the start of the night and its middle, to make ease for the Muslims."
"15781","682 - Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ayshun narrated to us, Abu Qatadah al-Harrani narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdallah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr at the start of the night, its middle and its end."
"15782","Yazid ibn Sharik al-Taymi from Abu Masud. 683 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: While I was beating a slave boy of mine, I heard a voice behind me: Know, Abu Masud, know, Abu Masud, three times. So I turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: By Allah, Allah is more able over you than you over this boy. So I swore never to beat a slave of mine again."
"15783","684 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shubah and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Masud, who said: While I was beating a slave boy of mine with the whip, I heard a voice behind me: Know, Abu Masud. I could not think from anger until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near to me. When I saw him, the whip fell from my hand. He said: Know, Abu Masud, that Allah is more able over you than you. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never beat a servant again."
"15784","685 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Masud, who said: While I was beating a slave boy of mine, I heard a voice behind me: Know, Abu Masud. So I turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The whip fell from my hand out of awe of him. He said: Indeed by Allah, Allah is more able over you than you over this boy."
"15785","686 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abdallah al-Hadrami said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Masud, who said: While I was beating a slave boy of mine, I heard a voice behind me: Know, Abu Masud. So I turned, and there he was, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned something similar."
"15786","Iyad ibn Iyad from Abu Masud. 687 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from a man - Sufyan said: I think him Iyad ibn Iyad - from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Among you are hypocrites; whoever I name, let him stand. So thirty-six stood. Then he said: Among you, or from you; so ask Allah for well-being. Then Umar passed by a man he knew and said: What is your matter? He informed him of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said. He said: Away with you all day."
"15787","Abu al-Jahm from Abu Masud. 688 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent him as a collector, said: Look, Abu Masud; let me not find you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a grumbling camel from the charity camels on your back, which you misappropriated. He said: I will not go in this mission of mine. He said: Then I will not compel you."
"15788","689 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu Masud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, then said: Look, Abu Masud; let me not find you on the Day of Resurrection coming with a grumbling charity camel on your back, which you misappropriated. I said: Then I will not go. He said: Then I will not compel you."
"15789","Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali from Abu Masud. 690 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali, who said: I entered upon Abu Masud, Ubayy ibn Kab and Thabit ibn Zayd, while slave girls were beating a drum of theirs and singing. I said: Do you approve of this while you are Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: It has been permitted for us at weddings, and weeping over the dead without wailing."
"15790","691 - Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad, who said: I attended a feast in which were Abu Masud and Qarazah ibn Kab, with singing girls. I said: Glory be to Allah, do you do this while you are Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and men of Badr? They said: Singing at weddings and weeping without wailing have been permitted for us."
"15791","al-Aswad ibn Hilal from Abu Masud. 692 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Ashath ibn Sulaym, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abu Masud, who said: It is not of the Sunnah to pray before the imam comes out on Eid day."
"15792","Nuaym ibn Dajajah from Abu Masud. 693 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqbal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us. (Ha) Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Nuaym ibn Dajajah, who said: We were with Ali when Uqbah Abu Masud came to him. Ali said to him: Do I not see you giving people verdicts? He said: Indeed I tell them that the later is worse. He said: Narrate to us what you heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about the hundred. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No hundred years come upon people while on earth an eye blinks. Ali said: You erred; he only said it about those who were then on the face of the earth, and is there ease and joy except after the hundred."
"15793","Fulfalah al-Jufi from Abu Masud. 694 - Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah al-Dhuhli narrated to us, who said: Fulfalah al-Jufi narrated to me, who said: Abu Masud said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and hardship struck the people until I saw gloom on the faces of the Muslims and joy on the faces of the hypocrites. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: By Allah, the sun will not set until Allah brings you provision. Uthman knew that Allah and His Messenger would speak truth, so Uthman bought forty mounts with the food on them, and directed nine of them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: What is this? They said: Uthman gifted it to you. Joy was seen on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gloom on the faces of the hypocrites. I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen, supplicating for Uthman with a supplication I never heard him supplicate for anyone before him nor after him: O Allah, grant Uthman; O Allah, do for Uthman."
"15794","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abu Masud. 695 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Salit al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden, then said: There will now enter upon you a man of Paradise. Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered. Then he said: There will now enter upon you a man of Paradise. Then Umar entered. Then he said: There will now enter upon you a man of Paradise; O Allah, make him Ali. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, entered."
"15795","Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn Masud from Abu Masud. 696 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, as for greeting you we have known it, so how do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim; O Allah, bless Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim."
"15796","Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn Zayd from Abu Masud. 697 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Nuaym ibn Abdallah al-Mujmir, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn Zayd informed him, that Abu Masud al-Ansari informed him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and sat with us in the gathering of Sad ibn Ubadah. Bashir ibn Sad, father of al-Numan ibn Bashir, said: Allah commanded us to send blessings upon you, so how do we send blessings upon you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent until we wished he had not asked him. Then he said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim among the worlds; indeed You are Praiseworthy. And the greeting as you learned."
"15797","698 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn Zayd, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he sat before him and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as for greeting you we have known it, but as for sending blessings upon you, inform us of it, how do we send blessings upon you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until we wished the man who asked him had not asked him. Then he said: When you send blessings upon me, say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"15798","Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani from Abu Masud. 699 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zurah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: We discussed standing at funerals in the presence of Ali, and Abu Masud said: We have continued to do it. Ali said: He spoke the truth; that, and you are witnesses."
"15799","Humam ibn al-Harith from Abu Masud. 700 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Humam ibn al-Harith, who said: Hudhayfah prayed in al-Madain on a bench, with Uqbah ibn Amr praying behind him. He took Uqbah by his garment and pulled him until he stepped back. Then he stood, and when he finished he said: Do you not remember this, and it was forbidden? He said: Yes, I remembered."
"15800","701 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Humam ibn al-Harith, that Hudhayfah prayed with his companions on a bench in al-Madain, and Abu Masud brought him down. When he finished his prayer he said: Did you not know that we were forbidden this? He said: Yes, I remembered when you brought me down."
"15801","702 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Humam ibn al-Harith, who said: Hudhayfah prayed in al-Madain, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15802","Abu Thawr al-Huddani - a clan of Murad - from Abu Masud. 703 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from al-Amash. (Ha) al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Thawr al-Huddani, who said: I was brought to Hudhayfah and Abu Masud in the mosque, while Abu Masud was saying: By Allah, I did not think it would exceed its two heels without a cupping-glass of blood being shed in it. Hudhayfah said: But I knew it would exceed its two heels without a cupping-glass of blood being shed in it; a man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever, and sleeps a believer and wakes a disbeliever, so his heart turns and his backside overcomes him; he fights tribulation today and Allah kills him tomorrow. Then Abu Masud said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us about tribulation."
"15803","704 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Utulli narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us. (Ha) Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us, both from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Thawr al-Huddani, who said: I was brought to Hudhayfah and Abu Masud, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15804","705 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Umarah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharazah narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Harun ibn Sad, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Thawr al-Huddani - a clan of Murad - who said: I was brought to Hudhayfah and Abu Masud while they were in the mosque of Kufah in the days of al-Jarah, when people did to Said ibn al-As what they did. Abu Masud was teaching the people and saying: By Allah, I do not think it will return upon its heels until there is blood in it. Hudhayfah said: By Allah, it will indeed return upon its heels without a cupping-glass of blood in it. I know nothing in it today except what I knew while Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive, and Harun ibn Sad did not mention Abu al-Bakhtari in his hadith."
"15805","Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi from Abu Masud. 706 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us. (Ha) Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us; both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would one of you be unable to recite a third of the Quran in the morning? That weighed heavily upon them, so he said: Allah, the One, the Eternal, is a third of the Quran."
"15806","707 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Can none of you recite one third of the Qur'an every night?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, which of us can bear that? He said: ""{Say: He is Allah, the One.""}"
"15807","708 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Can none of you - or: is none of you able - to recite one third of the Qur'an?"" So we spoke to him about that, and he said: ""{Say: He is Allah, the One.""}"
"15808","709 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, Abu Jabir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Mas'ud al-Badri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Can none of you recite one third of the Qur'an in a night?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, can we manage one third of the Qur'an? He said: ""Can none of you manage {Say: He is Allah, the One}?"""
"15809","'Amir al-Sha'bi, from Abu Mas'ud. 710 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mujalid, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr Abu Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised us at the foot of al-'Aqabah on the day of sacrifice, while we were seventy men. 'Uqbah said: I was the youngest of them in age. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: ""Be brief in the sermon, for I fear the disbelievers of Quraysh for you."" So we said: O Messenger of Allah, ask for your Lord, and ask for yourself, and ask for your Companions, and tell us what reward we shall have from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and from you. He said: ""As for what I ask for my Lord, that you believe in Him and associate nothing with Him; and as for what I ask for myself, I ask you to obey me so I may guide you to the path of rectitude; and I ask of you, for me and my Companions, that you share with us what you possess, and that you protect us as you protect yourselves. If you do that, Paradise from Allah and from me is yours."" He said: So we extended our hands and pledged allegiance to him."
"15810","Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud, from his father. 711 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: We were with 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and he delayed the 'Asr prayer, so 'Urwah said to him: Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Ansari narrated to me that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah once delayed the prayer - meaning 'Asr - so Abu Mas'ud said to him: By Allah, O Mughirah, you know that Jibril, peace be upon him, was sent down and prayed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and the people prayed with him; then he came down and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and the people prayed with him, until he counted five prayers. 'Umar said to him: Consider what you say, O 'Urwah - and indeed it is Jibril who laid down the time of prayer. 'Urwah said to him: That is how Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud narrated to me. He said: And 'Umar kept knowing the time of prayer by a sign until he left this world."
"15811","712 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab narrated to me that he heard 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz asking 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and 'Urwah said: Al-Mughirah delayed the 'Asr prayer while he was over al-Kufah, so Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari came to him and said: What is this, O Mughirah? By Allah, you know: Jibril came down and prayed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and the people prayed - five prayers, he kept saying - then he said: ""Thus I was commanded."" 'Umar said to 'Urwah: Know what you are saying, for it is Jibril who established the time of prayer. 'Urwah said: That is how Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud used to narrate from his father."
"15812","713 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, he said: I read to Malik ibn Anas. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us. (H). And 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz delayed the prayer one day, so 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr came to him and told him that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah delayed the prayer one day while he was in al-Kufah, so Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari came to him and said: O Mughirah, do you not know that Jibril, peace be upon him, came down and prayed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then he said: ""By this I was commanded""? 'Umar said to 'Urwah: Know what you narrate, O 'Urwah - was it Jibril who established for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the time of prayer? 'Urwah said: That is how Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud used to narrate from his father."
"15813","714 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us. (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. (H). And 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz delayed the prayer one day, so 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came down and led me in prayer, so I prayed with him; then he came down and led me, so I prayed with him; then he came down and led me, so I prayed with him, until he counted the five prayers."" 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz said to him: Fear Allah, O 'Urwah, and consider what you say. 'Urwah said: Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud informed me of it, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and the wording is al-Humaydi's."
"15814","715 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us. (H). And al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, he said: I heard Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Ansari saying: I heard Abu Mas'ud saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came down and led me in prayer, so I prayed with him; then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him"" - and he counted five prayers on his fingers."
"15815","716 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us. (H). And 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-'Utbi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihab, that they were at the gathering of 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, and with them was 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, when the caller summoned to the 'Asr prayer, so he led me in prayer before we prayed it; and when they returned, 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Did you know that Jibril, peace be upon him, came down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayed with him, and informed him of the time of prayer? 'Umar said: What are you saying, O 'Abdullah? 'Urwah said thereupon: Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Ansari informed me, from Abu Mas'ud, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came down upon me and I prayed with him; then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him."" Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying the midday prayer when the sun declined, sometimes delaying it in intense heat; and 'Asr while the sun was white and high, so that a man could walk until he would leave it for Dhu al-Hulayfah, six miles before sunset; and he would pray Maghrib when the sun set, and 'Isha when the horizon darkened, and Fajr in the darkness before dawn; then one day he prayed it bright, then he never returned to praying it bright until Allah took him - and the wording is Abu Salih's."
"15816","717 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Adi narrated to us, Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, and 'Uqayl, and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he informed him, from Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud, from his father Abu Mas'ud, that he said to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, when he prayed 'Asr late in the evening: By Allah, you know, O Mughirah, that Jibril, peace be upon him, came down and prayed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed; then he said: ""Thus I was commanded."""
"15817","718 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ayyub ibn 'Utbah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Hazm narrated to us, that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr used to narrate to 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz - when he was then governor of al-Madinah in the time of al-Hajjaj and al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Malik, a time in which they used to delay the prayer - so 'Urwah narrated to 'Umar, he said: Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari narrated to me - or: Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud, both of whom had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the sun declined and said: O Muhammad, pray Zuhr. So he stood and prayed. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him when the shadow of everything was like itself and said: O Muhammad, pray 'Asr. So he stood and prayed. Then he came to him when the sun set and said: O Muhammad, pray Maghrib. So he prayed. Then he came to him when the red twilight vanished and said: O Muhammad, stand and pray 'Isha. So he stood and prayed. Then he came to him when dawn split and said: O Muhammad, pray Fajr. So he stood and prayed. Then he came to him the next day when the shadow of everything was like itself and said: O Muhammad, stand and pray Zuhr. So he stood and prayed Zuhr. Then he came to him when the shadow of everything was twice itself and said: O Muhammad, pray 'Asr. So he stood and prayed. Then he came to him at the first time when the sun set and said: O Muhammad, pray Maghrib. So he prayed. Then he came to him after an hour of the night had passed and said: O Muhammad, stand and pray. Then he came to him when it was bright and said: O Muhammad, pray Fajr. So he stood and prayed. Then he said: What is between these two is the time."
"15818","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Mas'ud. 719 - Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Raja' al-'Abbadani narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Asid, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: I was right before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the pilgrimage, and the foam of his she-camel was falling on my back, and I heard him saying: ""Render to every holder of a right his right; the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone; and whoever allies himself to other than his masters, or claims descent from other than his father, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people - neither sarf nor 'adl will be accepted from him."""
"15819","'Ubayd ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Abu Mas'ud. 720 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Qasim ibn al-Harith, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: ""This authority will remain among you, and you will be its holders, so long as you do not innovate; but if you do that, Allah will set over you the wickedest of His creation, and they will strip you as a branch is stripped."""
"15820","721 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (H). And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn 'Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Qasim ibn al-Harith, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: ""This authority will remain among you, and you will be its holders."""
"15821","722 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and al-Hasan ibn 'Ulayl al-'Anbari, and Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi, and 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawahah al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, they said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Qasim, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Quraysh: ""This authority will remain among you, and you will be its holders, so long as you do not commit offenses; then He will set over you the wickedest of His creation, and they will strip you as a branch is stripped."""
"15822","Dhakwan Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Mas'ud. 723 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Asad narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Dhakwan, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I do a deed and conceal it, then it appears, and I rejoice at it. He said: ""Two rewards are written for you: the reward of secrecy and the reward of openness."""
"15823","Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from Abu Mas'ud. 724 - Al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hazm, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""Stand and pray"" - that was when the sun declined, when the sun moved - so he stood and prayed Zuhr, four units; then he came to him when his shadow was like him and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed 'Asr, four units; then he came to him when the sun set and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed Maghrib, three units; then he came to him when the twilight vanished and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed the last 'Isha, four units; then he came to him when dawn broke and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed Fajr, two units. Then he came to him the next day at Zuhr when his shadow was like him and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed Zuhr, four units; then he came to him when his shadow was twice him and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed 'Asr, four units; then he came to him at the first time when the sun set and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed Maghrib, three units; then he came to him after the twilight had gone and it had darkened and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed the last 'Isha, four units; then he came to him after dawn rose and it was bright and said: Stand and pray - so he prayed Fajr, two units. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, said to him: ""What is between these two is prayer."""
"15824","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, from Abu Mas'ud. 725 - 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Nu'aym ibn 'Abdullah al-Mujmir, that Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari informed him, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were in the gathering of Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, so Bashir ibn Sa'd said to him: Allah has commanded us to send blessings upon you, O Messenger of Allah - so how do we send blessings upon you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent until we wished he had not asked him. Then he said: ""Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim; and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim among the worlds. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And as for the greeting of peace, you already know it."""
"15825","Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud. 726 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"15826","727 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, from al-Layth. (H). And al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him that he heard Abu Mas'ud 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"15827","728 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us. (H). And 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, that he heard Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrating from Abu Mas'ud 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"15828","729 - 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zabalah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah and Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi 'Atiq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Abu Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"15829","730 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"15830","731 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus, al-Layth, and Malik informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"15831","732 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him that Abu Mas'ud 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the price of a dog, the fee of a soothsayer, and the dowry of a prostitute."
"15832","733 - Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim al-'Anbari narrated to us, 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Kurayzi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, that he narrated to them, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud, he said: The first of the Emigrants to arrive in al-Madinah was Mus'ab ibn 'Umayr, and he was the first to lead them in Friday prayer there, gathering them before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, and he prayed with them."
"15833","Hakim ibn Aflah, from Abu Mas'ud. 734 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, my father narrated to me, from Hakim ibn Aflah, from Abu Mas'ud al-Badri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: ""A Muslim owes his brother four duties: when he invites him, to answer him; when he dies, to attend him; when he falls ill, to visit him; and to say Yarhamuk Allah to him when he sneezes."""
"15834","'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, kunya Abu Hammad. He used to reside in Egypt. Description of 'Uqbah and his reports. 735 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Aqil, my grandfather and my father narrated to me that they saw 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani dyeing with black."
"15835","736 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abu 'Ushanah narrated to us, that he saw 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani dyeing with black, and saying: He said: And he was a poet."
"15836","737 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from 'Umarah ibn Sa'd al-Tujibi, that when death came to 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: O my sons, I forbid you three things, so guard them: do not accept hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from a trustworthy one; do not take on debt even if you wear a cloak; and do not write poetry that keeps your hearts occupied from the Qur'an."
"15837","738 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Hakam al-Balawi, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, he said: I came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab on Friday wearing leather socks, and he said to me: O 'Uqbah, when did you put them on? I said: On Friday. He said: And today is Friday? I said: Yes. He said: You are right."
"15838","What 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir transmitted; those Companions who narrated from him. Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir. 739 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us. (H). And Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir. (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from 'Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and I hastened to him and took his hand - or he hastened to me and took my hand - and he said: ""O 'Uqbah, shall I not tell you of the best character of the people of this world and the Hereafter? Join ties with whoever cuts you, give to whoever deprives you, and pardon whoever wrongs you. Whoever wishes his provision to be extended and his lifespan prolonged, let him fear Allah and join his kin."" And the wording is from the hadith of Ibn Abi Maryam."
"15839","740 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Abu 'Abd al-Malik, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me the most excellent deeds. He said: ""To give to whoever deprives you, to join whoever cuts you, and to pardon whoever wrongs you."""
"15840","741 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us. (H). And Abu Zayd narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir. (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from 'Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and said: What is salvation? He said: ""O 'Uqbah, hold your tongue, let your house suffice you, and weep over your sin."""
"15841","742 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, both from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, from Abu 'Abd al-Malik al-Shami - I think - from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Shall I not tell you of the best three surahs revealed in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Furqan?"" I said: Teach me, O Messenger of Allah, from what Allah taught you. So he recited {Say: He is Allah, the One} and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak} and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind}: ""If you can, do not spend a night without reciting them, and let no day pass you without reciting them."""
"15842","743 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from his father, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the believer's salvation? He said: ""Guard your tongue, let your house suffice you, and weep over your error."""
"15843","Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir. 744 - Al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Huraym ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sinan ibn Salamah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I perform Hajj on behalf of my mother, who has died? He said: ""Tell me: if your mother owed a debt and you paid it, would it not be accepted from you?"" She said: Yes. So he commanded her to perform Hajj on her behalf. And a woman came and said: Shall I perform Hajj with my son while he is nursing? He said: ""Yes."""
"15844","745 - Hajjaj ibn 'Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salamah narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his sister, who had vowed to walk to the Ka'bah. He said: ""Allah is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a camel as sacrifice."""
"15845","Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani, from 'Uqbah. 746 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ka'b ibn 'Alqamah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Shammasah, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."""
"15846","747 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rashdin narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ka'b ibn 'Alqamah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Shammasah, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."""
"15847","748 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Bishr, from Ibn Shammasah, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."""
"15848","749 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, narrated to us, he said: Ka'b ibn 'Alqamah narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."""
"15849","750 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me that Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed him that Abu al-Khayr narrated to him, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah, and she ordered me to seek a ruling for her, so I sought a ruling for her from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Let her walk and ride."" And Abu al-Khayr would never part from 'Uqbah."
"15850","751 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Rashdin ibn Sa'd, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The daughter of 'Amir vowed to walk to the House, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let her walk and ride."""
"15851","752 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us. (H). And al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The most rightful of conditions to fulfill are those by which you made private parts lawful."""
"15852","753 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most rightful of conditions to fulfill is that by which you made conditions lawful."""
"15853","754 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dharra' narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Yazid and Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed the most rightful of conditions you fulfill are those by which you made women's private parts lawful"" - or he said: ""by which private parts were made lawful."""
"15854","755 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Indeed the most rightful of conditions to fulfill is that by which you made private parts lawful."""
"15855","756 - Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Abu al-Khayr narrated to him, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Indeed the most rightful of conditions to fulfill are those by which you made private parts lawful."""
"15856","757 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, and my father narrated to me, from his father, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Indeed the most rightful of conditions to fulfill is that by which you made private parts lawful."""
"15857","758 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a silk outer garment, then removed it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed in it, then removed it? He said: ""This is not of the clothing of the God-fearing."""
"15858","759 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that he said: A silk outer garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he wore it, then prayed in it; then he turned and pulled it off forcefully as one displeased with it, then said: ""This is not befitting for the God-fearing."""
"15859","760 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us. (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: A silk outer garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he wore it and prayed; when he gave the salutation, he pulled it off violently, then cast it aside. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you wore it and prayed in it. He said: ""This is not befitting for the God-fearing."""
"15860","761 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him sheep and he divided them among his Companions as sacrifices, but a young goat remained. He mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Sacrifice it yourself."""
"15861","762 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of entering upon women."" A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the in-law? He said: ""The in-law is death."""
"15862","763 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not enter upon women."" A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the in-law? He said: ""The in-law is death."""
"15863","764 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not converse in the presence of women."""
"15864","765 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Do not enter upon women."" It was said: The in-law? He said: ""The in-law is death."""
"15865","766 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: We said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You send us out and we lodge with people who do not host us - what do you think of that? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: ""If you lodge with people and they provide for you what befits a guest, accept it; but if they do not do so, take from them the right of the guest that is due to them."""
"15866","767 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day and prayed over the people of Uhud his prayer over the dead, then turned to the pulpit and said: ""I am your forerunner, and I am a witness over you. By Allah, I am now looking at my Basin, and I have been given the keys of the earth. By Allah, I do not fear that you will associate partners after me, but I fear that you will compete over it."""
"15867","768 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us. (H). And Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the slain of Uhud after eight years, like one bidding farewell to the living and the dead; then he ascended the pulpit and said: ""I am before you, a forerunner, and I am a witness over you; your appointed meeting is the Basin - indeed I am looking at it while in this station of mine. I do not fear that you will associate partners, but I fear this world for you, that you will compete over it."" 'Uqbah said: It was the last look I cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - each of them close to his companion's hadith, and al-Layth ibn Sa'd did not mention: eight years."
"15868","769 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the slain of Uhud, then ascended the pulpit like one bidding farewell to the living and the dead, and said: ""I am your forerunner at the Basin; its width is what is between Aylah and al-Juhfah. I do not fear that you will associate partners after me, but I fear this world for you, that you will compete over it and fail and perish as those before you perished."" It was the last time I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque."
"15869","770 - Abu 'Arubah al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the slain of Uhud, then turned and sat on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""O people, I am before you, a forerunner, and I am a witness over you. By Allah, I am looking at my Basin, while I am in my station; its expanse is what is between al-Juhfah and Aylah. By Allah, I do not fear that you will associate partners after me; I have been given the keys of the treasuries of this world and the treasuries of the earth - I only fear for you that you will compete over it."" Then he entered and did not come out of his house until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took him."
"15870","771 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Harmalah ibn 'Imran narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every person is in the shade of his charity until judgment is passed among people"" - or he said: ""until it is judged among people."" Yazid said: And Abu al-Khayr would not let a day pass him without giving charity - a cake, or a bean, or such - he named something."
"15871","772 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that a boy said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My mother left jewelry - shall I give it in charity on her behalf? He said: ""Did she command you to do that?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then keep it for yourself."""
"15872","773 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died and left jewelry without bequeathing - will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: ""Keep your wealth for yourself."""
"15873","774 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Upon you is this blessed tree, olive oil - so treat yourselves with it, for it is a cure for piles."""
"15874","775 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Our Lord is All-Hearing, All-Seeing"" - and he pointed with his hand to his eyes."
"15875","776 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting this verse at the end of al-Nur, placing his two fingers beneath his eyes, saying: ""{All-Seer of everything}."""
"15876","777 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The callers to prayer will have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection."""
"15877","778 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a handful of dates and said: ""What an excellent sahur for the Muslim."""
"15878","779 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Recite these two verses at the end of Surah al-Baqarah, for my Lord has given them to me from beneath the Throne."""
"15879","780 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Recite these two verses at the end of Surah al-Baqarah, for I was given them from beneath the Throne."""
"15880","781 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith ibn Suwayd al-Hasib al-Mahri informed me, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that he said: They disputed over the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah: {The Messenger believes in what was revealed to him from his Lord} to its end - for Allah singled out Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with them."
"15881","782 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""No deed of a day passes but it is sealed upon it; when the believer falls ill, the angels say: Our Lord, such-and-such Your servant - You have confined him. So He says: Gather for him the like of his deeds until he recovers or dies."""
"15882","783 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The likeness of one who commits evil deeds and then does good deeds is like a man wearing a tight coat of mail that nearly strangles him; then he does a good deed and a ring comes loose, then he does another and another ring comes loose, until he comes out onto open ground."""
"15883","784 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The likeness of one who commits evil deeds and then does good deeds is like a man wearing a tight coat of mail that has strangled him; each time he does a good deed a ring breaks off, then another, until he comes out onto open ground."""
"15884","785 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-'Abdi narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When I was taken up to heaven, I entered the Garden of Eden, and an apple fell into my hand; when I placed it in my hand, it split open upon a wide-eyed houri, pleasing - the lashes of her eyes like the foremost feathers of eagles' wings. I said to her: To whom do you belong? She said: I belong to the caliph after you."""
"15885","786 - Khalaf ibn 'Amr al-'Ukbari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever a man embraces Islam at his hands, Paradise becomes due for him."""
"15886","787 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Ya'la ibn 'Ata' al-Muharibi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Charity extinguishes the heat of the graves."""
"15887","788 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith, Ibn Lahi'ah, and al-Hasan ibn Thawban narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Charity extinguishes from its people the heat of the graves; the believer will only be shaded on the Day of Resurrection in the shade of his charity."""
"15888","789 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was riding his white mule - so I placed my hand on his foot and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite. He said: ""You will never recite anything more effective with Allah than {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak}."""
"15889","790 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, you have grown grey. He said: ""Hud and its sisters have turned me grey."""
"15890","791 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us commits a sin? He said: ""It is written against him."" Then he said: Then he seeks forgiveness for it and repents? He said: ""He is forgiven and rewarded for it; and Allah does not tire until you tire."""
"15891","792 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Abu al-Khayr narrated to him that Abu Tamim al-Jayshani stood and bowed two units before Maghrib, so I said to 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir: Look at this - what prayer is he praying? He turned and said: ""This is a prayer we used to pray in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"15892","793 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, that Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed him, he said: I heard Abu al-Khayr saying: I saw Abu Tamim al-Jayshani bowing two units when he heard the Maghrib call before the prayer, so I came intending to stop him, and 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir said: ""We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"15893","794 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Misri, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn 'Abdullah al-Yazani - I think from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things: whoever is saved from them is saved - whoever is saved when a believer is killed is saved; whoever is saved when a caliph is killed wrongfully, while he is patient and renders the right from himself, is saved; and whoever is saved from the trial of the Dajjal is saved."""
"15894","795 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Kurdus ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""No man sees a private fault of his brother and conceals it but Allah will conceal him and admit him to Paradise."""
"15895","796 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Abu al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If there is healing in anything, it is in the cut of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or cauterization striking pain; and I dislike cauterization and do not love it."""
"15896","'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir. 797 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani saying: There are three hours in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid us to pray or to bury our dead: when the sun rises appearing until it ascends; when the midday stander stands until the sun declines; and when the sun inclines toward setting until it sets."
"15897","798 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: There are three hours in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid us to pray in them or to bury our dead in them. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"15898","799 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were in al-Suffah and said: ""Which of you would love to go out to Buthan or al-'Aqiq and bring back every day two large-humped, excellent she-camels and take them?"" We said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us would love that. He said: ""Should not one of you go out to the mosque and learn two verses from the Book of Allah - better for him than two she-camels; and three better for him than three; and four better for him than four; and their numbers of camels on the days of Mina."""
"15899","800 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Qabath. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl and al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, they said: 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Qabath ibn Razin narrated to me, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while we were studying the Qur'an and said: ""Learn the Book of Allah, spread it, and chant it; for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it slips away more swiftly than pregnant camels from their hobbles."""
"15900","801 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Learn the Qur'an, chant it, and acquire it; for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it slips away more swiftly than pregnant camels from their hobbles."""
"15901","802 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Qabath ibn Razin narrated to me, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15902","803 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, I heard my father narrating from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The day of 'Arafah, the day of sacrifice, and the days of Tashriq are our festival, O people of Islam; they are days of eating and drinking."""
"15903","804 - Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Salih al-Hadrami narrated to me, from Musa ibn 'Ulayy, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah; that reached 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he placed dust on his head and said: Allah pays no heed to you, O son of al-Khattab, after this. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came down and said: ""Allah, Exalted is He, commands you to take Hafsah back, out of mercy for 'Umar."""
"15904","805 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Asad ibn Musa informed us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will tell us where our milch camels are?"" A man stood and said: I will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""What is your name?"" He said: Sakhr - or Jandal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Sit."" Then he said: ""Who will tell us where our milch camels are?"" A man stood and said: I will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""What is your name?"" He said: Ya'ish. He said: ""Tell us where our milch camels are."""
"15905","806 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: When Ibrahim died, the sun eclipsed, so the people said: The sun eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for anyone's death nor his life. When you see that, hasten to prayer."""
"15906","807 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not force your sick to eat, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink."""
"15907","808 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Ulayy, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of the best of your workers and the worst of them?"" They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""The best of them for you are those whom you love and who love you, for whom you supplicate to Allah and who supplicate to Allah for you; and the worst of them for you are those whom you hate and who hate you, against whom you supplicate to Allah and who supplicate to Allah against you."" They said: Shall we not fight them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""No - call them, so long as they fast and pray."""
"15908","809 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, my uncle Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us. (H). And Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you intend to raid, buy a horse with a white blaze on its forehead, white-marked legs, with the right foreleg free of marking; then you will be safe and gain booty."""
"15909","810 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Bishr ibn Thabit narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, from his father, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from an evil day, an evil night, an evil hour, an evil companion, and an evil neighbor in the abode of residence."""
"15910","811 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, Yazid ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Ru'ayni and Abu Marhum 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to recite al-Mu'awwidhat after every prayer."
"15911","812 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Hunayn ibn Abi Hakim, from 'Ulayy ibn Rabah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Recite al-Mu'awwidhat after every prayer."""
"15912","813 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of a man called Dhu al-Bijadayn: ""He is oft-returning to Allah"" - and that was because he would frequently remember Allah with the Qur'an and supplication."
"15913","814 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, 'Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These lineages of yours are not grounds for insulting anyone; you are but the children of Adam - a trifle of a sa' that you would fill. No one has merit over another except by religion or righteous deed. It suffices a man to be foul-mouthed, obscene, miserly, and given to swearing."""
"15914","Abu Qabil Hayy ibn Hani' al-Ma'afiri, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir. 815 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""What I fear most for my ummah is the Book and milk: as for milk, some people will pursue it and abandon Friday and the congregations; and as for the Book, it will be opened to some people, and they will dispute with it against those who believe."""
"15915","816 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What I fear most - or: the most fearful thing I fear - for my ummah is milk and the Book."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with milk? He said: ""They leave the congregations and abandon the Fridays."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with the Book? He said: ""It is opened to some people and they recite it, then dispute with it."""
"15916","817 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Malik ibn al-Khayr al-Ziyadi narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Some of my ummah will perish over the Book and milk."" 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir said: I said: Who are the people of the Book? He said: ""A people who learn the Book of Allah and dispute with it against those who believe."" I said: Who are the people of milk, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""A people who follow desires and neglect prayers."""
"15917","818 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Samh narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What I fear most for my ummah are two things: that they follow the verses and desires, and abandon the Qur'an and the prayers - that the hypocrites learn it and dispute with it against the people of knowledge."""
"15918","Abu al-Mus'ab Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah. 819 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, that Abu al-Mus'ab Mishrah ibn Ha'an al-Ma'afiri narrated to him that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani saying: ""It is written, for every gesture a man gestures with his hand in prayer, for every finger a good deed or a degree."""
"15919","Khalid ibn 'Ubayd, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an. 820 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Khalid ibn 'Ubayd, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever hangs a shell bead, may Allah give him no protection; and whoever hangs an amulet, may Allah give him no completion."""
"15920","Bakr ibn 'Amr, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an. 821 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Yazid informed us, Bakr ibn 'Amr narrated to me that he heard Mishrah ibn Ha'an saying: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will emerge peoples from my ummah who drink the Qur'an as they drink milk."""
"15921","822 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Bakr ibn 'Amr, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Had there been a prophet after me, it would have been 'Umar."""
"15922","823 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Bakr ibn 'Amr, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The people of Yemen have the tenderest and softest hearts, and are most obedient."""
"15923","824 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Wahbullah ibn Rashid al-Ma'afiri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh ibn Bakr ibn 'Amr al-Ma'afiri narrated to us, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Filth is seventy parts: for the Berbers sixty-nine parts, and for jinn and men one part."""
"15924","Al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Mishrah. 825 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abu Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of the borrowed billy-goat?"" They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""He is the muhallil; and Allah has cursed the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done."""
"15925","Abu 'Ushanah Hayy ibn Yu'min, from 'Uqbah. Harmalah ibn 'Imran al-Tujibi, from Abu 'Ushanah. 826 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Harmalah ibn 'Imran narrated to me, from Abu 'Ushanah al-Ma'afiri, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, feeding them, giving them drink, and clothing them, they will be for him a veil from the Fire."""
"15926","827 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Harmalah ibn 'Imran al-Tujibi and Ibn al-Had, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, feeding them, giving them drink, and clothing them, they will be for him a veil from the Fire."""
"15927","'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu 'Ushanah. 829 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us. (H). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Abu 'Ushanah al-Ma'afiri narrated to him that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever loses three of his loins and seeks reward with Allah for them"" - and Abu 'Ushanah once said: in the path of Allah, and another time did not say it - ""Paradise becomes due for him."""
"15928","830 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Harmalah ibn 'Imran and Ibn al-Had, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, they will be for him a screen from the Fire."""
"15929","831 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me. (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that Abu 'Ushanah narrated to him, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever performs ablution and gathers his clothes, then goes out to the mosque, his scribe writes for him ten good deeds for every step; and a person is in prayer so long as he awaits the prayer; and he is recorded among those praying from when he leaves his house until he returns."""
"15930","832 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu 'Ushanah, he narrated to him that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take a house in Hell."""
"15931","833 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu 'Ushanah, he narrated to him that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Your Lord marvels at a shepherd on a mountain peak calling the adhan for prayer and praying; so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Look at this servant of Mine - he calls the adhan and establishes the prayer out of fear of Me. I have forgiven My servant and admitted him to Paradise."""
"15932","834 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abu 'Ushanah narrated to him that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun will draw near to the earth on the Day of Resurrection, and people will sweat: some people's sweat will reach their ankles; some to mid-shin; some to their knees; some to their buttocks; some to the waist; some to their shoulders; some to their throats; and some it will bridle."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured, joining his fingers between his lips, he said: ""And some it will submerge."""
"15933","835 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid his family jewelry and silk, saying: ""If you love the jewelry and silk of Paradise, do not touch them in this world."""
"15934","836 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors."""
"15935","837 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Darraj, from Abu al-Qasim, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People are three: safe, gaining, and perishing."""
"15936","Al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, from Abu 'Ushanah. 838 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from al-Harith, from Zayd, from Abu al-Mus'ab, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr: ""When do you pray witr?"" He said: I pray two by two, then pray witr before I sleep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""A cautious believer."" And he said to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab: ""How do you pray witr?"" He said: I pray two by two, then sleep until I pray witr at the end of the night. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A strong believer."""
"15937","Ma'ruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami, from Abu 'Ushanah. 839 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ma'ruf ibn Suwayd al-Wa'ili, from Abu 'Ushanah, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying upon the pulpit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in al-Madinah while I was among sheep I tended, so I left them and went to him and said: Will you pledge me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""From whom are you?"" I told him, and he said: ""Which is dearer to you: a pledge of migration or a Bedouin pledge?"" I said: A pledge of migration. So he pledged me. Then he said: ""Whoever here is of Ma'add, let him stand?"" So I stood, and he said: ""Sit."" Then he said: ""Whoever here is of Ma'add, let him stand?"" So I stood, and he said: ""Sit."" Then he said it a third time, and I stood, and he said: ""Sit."" I said: Of whom are we, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""You are of Quda'ah, then of Malik ibn Himyar."""
"15938","840 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Fadalah ibn al-Fudayl ibn Fadalah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Ma'ruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, from Abu 'Ushanah, that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever here is of Ma'add, let him stand?"" Then he mentioned the like of it."
"15939","Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu 'Ushanah. 841 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us. (H). And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us. (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters."""
"15940","842 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When the servant purifies himself, then comes to the mosque observing the prayer, a book is written for him - ten good deeds for every step he takes to the mosque; and one sitting in it awaiting the prayer is like the devoutly obedient; and he is recorded among those praying from when he leaves his house until he returns to it."""
"15941","843 - Khayr ibn 'Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abu 'Ushanah, 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir said, saying: We do not say what he did not say. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in Hell. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Men of my ummah - one of them rises at night and strives with himself in purification, with a knot upon him; when he washes his feet a knot comes undone; when he washes his face a knot comes undone; when he wipes his head a knot comes undone. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Look at My servant striving with himself to ask Me - whatever My servant asks is his."""
"15942","844 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, that he heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun will draw near to the earth on the Day of Resurrection and people will sweat: some people's sweat will reach their knees; some will reach - I think he said - the buttocks; some will reach their shoulders; some will reach their upper arms; some will reach the middle of his mouth"" - and he gestured with his hand and bridled his mouth with it - ""he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spreading it thus"" - ""and some his sweat will cover."" And he struck his head with his hand."
"15943","845 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Naji narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us. (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people embraced Islam, and 'Amr ibn al-'As believed."""
"15944","846 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj distinguished by two prostrations? He said: ""Yes; whoever does not prostrate in them, let him not recite them."""
"15945","847 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-'Askari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, are there two prostrations in Surah al-Hajj? He said: ""Yes; if he does not prostrate them, let him not recite them."""
"15946","848 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us. (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every dead person, when he dies, his deed is sealed, except the one stationed in the path of Allah - for it flows for him until he is raised."""
"15947","849 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Recite al-Mu'awwidhatayn, for you will never recite the like of them."""
"15948","850 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Naji narrated to us. (H). And Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Had the Qur'an been in a skin, the Fire would not have eaten it."""
"15949","851 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Faith is Yemeni, and Mudar is at the tails of camels."""
"15950","852 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu 'Ushanah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors."""
"15951","853 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abbad al-Abbadani narrated (H). And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, both saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah Almighty marvels at a young man who has no youthful folly."
"15952","854 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, they will be a screen for him from the Fire."
"15953","855 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Your Lord marvels at a shepherd on a mountain peak who calls the adhan for prayer and performs the iqamah."
"15954","856 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate daughters, for they are comforting and precious."
"15955","857 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Naji narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Ushshanah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there were to be a prophet after me, Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) would be."
"15956","858 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Fayyad al-Raqqi narrated, Ashhab ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acts with deliberation gets it right or nearly so, and whoever hastens errs or nearly so."
"15957","859 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Najih narrated, my father informed me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah blesses with a blessing and wants it to remain, let him say often: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And why did you not, when you entered your garden, say: What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah."
"15958","Aslam Abu Imran al-Tujibi, from Uqbah. 860 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu Imran Aslam, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I followed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was riding, and I placed my hand on his foot and said: Teach me from Surah Hud or Surah Yusuf. He said: You will never recite anything more effective with Allah than: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak."
"15959","861 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while he was riding, and I placed my hand on his foot and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from Surah Hud or from Surah Yusuf. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Uqbah ibn Amir, you will never recite a surah dearer to Allah and more effective with Him than reciting: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, so if you can never miss it in a prayer, then do so."
"15960","862 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, both saying: We heard Yazid ibn Abi Habib saying, Abu Imran narrated to me, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I clung to the foot of the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me Surah Hud and Surah Yusuf. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Uqbah, you will never recite a surah dearer to Allah nor more effective than: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak."
"15961","863 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa narrated, both saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran who said: Uqbah ibn Amir led us in the Maghrib prayer and delayed it while we were at Constantinople, and Abu Ayyub al-Ansari was with us. Abu Ayyub said to him: Why do you delay this prayer while you are of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? One who did not accompany him will see you and think that is its time. We said: O Abu Ayyub, how did you pray it? He said: We used to pray it when the sun set, hastening it before the stars. Is it so, O Uqbah? He said: Yes."
"15962","Wahib ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Uqbah. 864 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Wahib ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I am Abu Hammad; I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever finds a Muslim upon a fault and conceals it, it is as if he brought a buried girl back to life from her grave."
"15963","Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 865 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa narrated, both saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Kab ibn Alqamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The expiation of a vow is the expiation of an oath."
"15964","866 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Kab ibn Alqamah, from Ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A vow is an oath, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"15965","867 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, that Ibn Shimashah narrated to him, that Uqbah ibn Amir stood in a prayer while sitting was due upon him, and the people said: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah. He understood what they meant, and when he completed his prayer he performed two prostrations while sitting, then said: I heard what you said; this is the Sunnah."
"15966","868 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shimashah who said: Uqbah ibn Amir led us in prayer and stood while sitting was due upon him. The people behind him said: Glory be to Allah, but he did not sit. When he finished he performed two prostrations while sitting, then said: I heard you saying: Glory be to Allah, so that I would sit, but that is not the Sunnah; the Sunnah is only what I did."
"15967","869 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will ever remain a band of my ummah fighting upon the truth, dominant over their enemy; the enmity of whoever opposes them will not harm them until the Hour comes to them while they are upon that."
"15968","870 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will ever remain a band of my ummah fighting upon the command of Allah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15969","871 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw the Fire, and I saw in it Imran ibn Hurthan reclining upon his bow; he used to rob the pilgrims. And I saw the Himyari woman, the owner of the cat."
"15970","872 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah al-Mahri, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and he lengthened the standing, though when he led us he used to lighten; I saw him reach out with his hand to take something, then he bowed after that. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salam, he sat and we sat around him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you realize that the length of my prayer and standing startled you? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and we heard you saying: O my Lord, while I am among them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, nothing you were promised of the Hereafter but was displayed to me in this station of mine, until the Fire was displayed to me; a spark from it came toward me until it faced this tent of mine, and I feared it would envelop you, so I said: O my Lord, while I am among them? Allah turned it away from you and it receded in pieces as if they were carpets. I took a glance and saw Imran ibn Hurthan ibn al-Harith, one of Banu Ghifar, reclining in Hell upon his bow, and I saw in it the Himyari woman, the owner of the cat which she tied up, neither feeding it nor giving it drink. Ahmad ibn Salih said: The correct form is Hurthan."
"15971","873 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is the brother of the believer; it is not lawful for a believer to outbid the sale of his brother until he leaves it, nor to propose over his engagement until he leaves it."
"15972","874 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir reporting from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None of you should outbid the sale of his brother, nor propose over his engagement."
"15973","875 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"15974","876 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim."
"15975","877 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; it is not lawful for a Muslim, if he sells his brother something containing a defect, except to make it clear to him."
"15976","878 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The collector of the toll-tax will not enter Paradise."
"15977","879 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The collector of the toll-tax will not enter Paradise."
"15978","880 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The collector of the toll-tax will not enter Paradise."
"15979","881 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Wahib ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who dies of pleurisy is a martyr."
"15980","882 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated (H). And Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Ya'qub, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimashah, that a man said to Uqbah ibn Amir: You go back and forth between these two targets while you are an old man and that is hard for you? Uqbah said: Were it not for words I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would not trouble myself with it: Whoever learns shooting in Mecca is not of us."
"15981","Dukhayn Abu al-Haytham, scribe of Uqbah, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 883 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Nashit, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, that he heard Abu al-Haytham Dukhayn, freedman of Uqbah ibn Amir, saying: We had neighbors who drank wine, and I forbade them but they did not desist, so I said to Uqbah: Our neighbors drink wine; I forbade them but they did not desist, and I am going to call the police for them. He said: Leave them; woe to you, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever sees a fault of a Muslim and conceals it, it is as if he brought a buried girl back to life from her grave."
"15982","884 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Nashit, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, from Abu al-Haytham, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sees a fault and conceals it is like one who brought a buried girl back to life from her grave."
"15983","885 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Mansur, from Dukhayn al-Hajari, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that ten came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance, and he pledged nine and withheld from one. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you pledged nine and withheld from this one? He said: This one has an amulet upon him. He put his hand in and cut it off, then pledged him."
"15984","886 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ammar ibn Umar ibn al-Mukhtar narrated (H). And Hakim ibn Yahya al-Mathuthi al-Basri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated, both saying: Sahl ibn Aslam al-Adawi narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Mansur narrated, from Dukhayn al-Hajari, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the sister of Uqbah vowed to walk to the House of Allah barefoot and uncovered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her and said: What is the matter with her? They said: She vowed to walk to the House of Allah barefoot and uncovered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Order her to cover herself and to ride and to perform the pilgrimage."
"15985","887 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, both saying: Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Nu'aym informed me, from Dukhayn al-Hajari, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah gathers the first and the last and judges between them and finishes judging between them, the believers will say: Our Lord has judged between us, so who will intercede for us with our Lord? Come with us to Adam, for he is our father, and Allah created him with His Hand and spoke to him. They will come to him and ask him to intercede for them, and he will say: Go to Nuh. They will come to Nuh, and he will direct them to Ibrahim. They will come to Ibrahim, and he will direct them to Musa. They will come to Musa, and he will direct them to Isa. Then they will come to Isa, and he will say: I will direct you to the unlettered Prophet. They will come to me, and Allah will permit me to stand, and my sitting-place will surge with the sweetest scent anyone ever smelled, until I come to my Lord, blessed and exalted, and He will grant me intercession and will make for me a light from the hair of my head to the nail of my foot. Then the disbelievers will say: The believers have found one to intercede for them, so who will intercede for us? They will say: It is none but Iblis; he is the one who led us astray. They will come to him and say: The believers have found one to intercede for them, so stand and intercede for us, for you are the one who led us astray. He will stand, and his sitting-place will surge with the foulest stench anyone ever smelled, then he will drive them to Hell, and at that he will say: And Satan will say when the matter is decided: Indeed Allah promised you a promise of truth, and I promised you and broke my promise to you."
"15986","888 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Zayd ibn Bishr al-Hadrami narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed me, from Umayr ibn Nu'aym al-Ru'ayni, from Mughirah ibn Nuhayk, from Dukhayn al-Hajari, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir reporting that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah eating with her left hand and said: What is the matter with her, eating with her left hand? Do I find her insolent? She said: O Messenger of Allah, there is a wound in my right hand. He said: Even if."
"15987","Iyas ibn Amir al-Ghafiqi, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 889 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi narrated, my uncle Iyas ibn Amir informed me, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, when: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Put it in your prostrations."
"15988","890 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi of Egypt narrated to me, from a man of his people whom he named, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: When this verse was revealed: So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it in your bowings. And when: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it in your prostrations. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed he said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most Great, three times, and when he prostrated he said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, three times."
"15989","891 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Musa ibn Ayyub, from Iyas ibn Amir, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: When: So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it in your bowings. And when: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it in your prostrations."
"15990","Ja'far ibn Abd Allah, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 892 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated (H). And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Ja'far ibn Abd Allah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is thrown from his mount is a martyr."
"15991","Abd Allah ibn Malik, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 893 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Abu Sa'id al-Ru'ayni, from Abd Allah ibn Malik, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that his sister vowed to walk barefoot and uncovered, so Uqbah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is free of need of your sister's hardship, so order her to cover herself and to ride and to fast three days."
"15992","894 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Abu Sa'id al-Yahsabi, from Abd Allah ibn Malik, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that his sister vowed to perform the pilgrimage walking and uncovered, so Uqbah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Order her to cover herself and to ride and to fast three days."
"15993","Abd Allah ibn Sharahil, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 895 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn Sharahil who said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No rider is alone on his journey with Allah and His remembrance but an angel rides behind him, and he is not alone with poetry and the like but a devil rides behind him."
"15994","Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 896 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ibn Ha'an, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that his sister vowed to walk to the House barefoot and uncovered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her ride and clothe herself and fast."
"15995","Al-Mughirah ibn Hind al-Hajari, from Uqbah. 897 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Rabi'ah al-Ru'ayni, from al-Mughirah ibn Hind al-Hajari, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He saw Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah eating with her left hand and said: What is the matter with her, eating with her left hand? She said: O Prophet of Allah, there is a wound in my right hand. He said to her: Even if... death of a cow, then plague seized it and killed it."
"15996","Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayl, from Uqbah. 898 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Harmalah ibn Imran informed me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayl narrated to me, my father narrated to me, saying: I was with Uqbah ibn Amir and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Men will recite the Qur'an and it will not pass their collarbones; they will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game."
"15997","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from Uqbah. 899 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour a black cloud will rise upon you from the west like a shield, and it will keep rising in the sky and spreading until it fills the sky, then a caller will call: O people! People will turn to one another: Did you hear? Some of them will say: Yes. Then he will call a second time: O people! The command of Allah has come, so do not seek to hasten it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, two men will spread a garment and never fold it, a man will leave his watering trough and never give drink from it again, and a man will milk his she-camel and never drink it."
"15998","900 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh informed me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Tha'labah al-Hadrami reporting that he heard Abu Hujayrah al-Akbar mentioning that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir mentioning from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Five - whoever is taken in any of them is a martyr: one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, one drowned in the path of Allah is a martyr, one who dies of plague in the path of Allah is a martyr, one who dies of a belly disease in the path of Allah is a martyr, and a woman dying in childbirth in the path of Allah is a martyr."
"15999","901 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya, secretary of al-Umari, narrated, Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muradi, from Abu Marwan, from Sahl ibn Alqamah, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir and Fadalah ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in major impurity, then bathe and fast."
"16000","Rabi'ah ibn Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 902 - Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Rabi'ah ibn Qays, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays without heedlessness, what came before it of his year will be expiated for him."
"16001","903 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from a man who narrated to him, from Rabi'ah ibn Qays, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays without heedlessness nor distraction, what came before it will be expiated for him."
"16002","Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayyah, from Uqbah. 904 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayyah al-Lakhmi who narrated to him, saying: I heard Maslamah ibn Mukhallad while he was sitting upon the pulpit saying: O people, do you not have in gold and linen what suffices you, while this man among you reports from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Stand, O Uqbah. Uqbah ibn Amir stood while I listened, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that I heard him saying: Whoever wears silk in this world will be deprived of wearing it in the Hereafter."
"16003","905 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated (H). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated, al-Firyabi narrated, Ibn Thawban narrated, from Abu Maryam, from Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayyah, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world, it is forbidden for him in the Hereafter."
"16004","Shu'ayb ibn Zur'ah, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 906 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Bakr ibn Amr (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi' ibn Yazid informed us, Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, Shu'ayb ibn Zur'ah narrated, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not frighten souls after their security. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that? He said: Debt."
"16005","Abu Ali al-Hamdani Thumamah ibn Shufi, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 907 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated, Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani Thumamah ibn Shufi, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant leads a people but he takes charge of what is upon them in their prayer; if he does well it is for him, and if he does badly it is for them and upon him."
"16006","908 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Isa informed me, Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani Thumamah ibn Shufi who said: We were with Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani and the prayer came, so we asked him to lead us and he refused us and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant leads a people but he takes charge of what is upon them in their prayer; if he does it well it is for him and for them, and if he does badly it is upon him and not upon them."
"16007","909 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16008","910 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated, Wahb ibn Khalid narrated, from Ibn Harmalah (H). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, Abu Ali al-Hamdani narrated to me - his dwelling one year was Alexandria - saying: I went out on a journey and Uqbah ibn Amir was with us, so we said to him: Lead us. He said: I will not do it; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever leads the people and gets the time right and completes the prayer, it is for him and for them; and whoever falls short of that in anything, it is upon him and not upon them."
"16009","911 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, both saying: Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani Thumamah ibn Shufi, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the pulpit reciting: And prepare for them what you can of power; verily power is shooting, verily power is shooting."
"16010","912 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh and Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated (H). Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, both saying: Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani who said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Lands will be opened for you, and Allah will suffice you, so let none of you fail to amuse himself with his arrow."
"16011","Uqbah ibn Muslim, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 913 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Harmalah ibn Imran narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Muslim, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see Allah giving the servant what he loves while he persists in his disobedience, that is only gradual enticement for him from Him. Then he quoted this verse: So when they forgot what they were reminded of, We opened for them the doors of everything, until when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly, and behold they were in despair. Then cut off was the remnant of the people who wronged, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"16012","914 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16013","Uncle of Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 915 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Aqil, my uncle narrated to me, Uqbah ibn Amir narrated, saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was speaking to his Companions, and he said: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays two rak'ahs, will be of his sins as on the day his mother bore him. I said: Praise be to Allah who granted me to hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16014","916 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad Abu Aqil informed me, that a cousin of his informed him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and completes his ablution, then raises his head to the sky and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him; he may enter through whichever he wills."
"16015","Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Uqbah. 917 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated (H). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, both saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, and Abu Uthman, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: Tending camels was our turn; my turn to tend them came, and I brought them back in the evening. I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing speaking to the people, and I caught of his words: There is none of you who performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then stands and prays two rak'ahs, turning to them with his face and heart, but Paradise becomes due for him."
"16016","Qays al-Judhami, from Uqbah. 918 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Qays al-Judhami, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a believing slave, she will be his ransom from the Fire."
"16017","919 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan ibn Qays al-Judhami, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever frees a believing slave, she will be his ransom."
"16018","920 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Qatadah, from Qays al-Judhami, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever frees a believing slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire, each limb for a limb."
"16019","Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 921 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first thing to speak of a man when mouths are sealed will be his thigh of the left leg."
"16020","922 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man approves of another man's guidance and deed, he is like him."
"16021","Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 923 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One who recites the Qur'an secretly is like one who gives charity secretly, and one who recites the Qur'an openly is like one who gives charity openly."
"16022","924 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16023","925 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated, Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet of Allah, blessings of Allah upon him, said: One who recites the Qur'an secretly is like one who gives charity secretly, and one who recites the Qur'an openly is like one who gives charity openly."
"16024","Al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 926 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated (H). And Bakr ibn Khalid ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, both saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated, from al-Ala' ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: I was leading the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in travel, and he said: O Uqbah, shall I not teach you the best two surahs ever recited? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, teach me. He taught me: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. He did not see me impressed by them. When he alighted he led the people in the dawn prayer with them, and when he finished his prayer he turned to me and said: O Uqbah, how did you find them?"
"16025","927 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated, Yahya ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from al-Qasim, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance Hell from him a journey of a hundred years."
"16026","928 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Uqbah ibn Amir - and he was the keeper of the grey mule of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he led in travels - who said: I led the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon his mount for a portion of the night. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make it kneel. I made it kneel, and he alighted from his mount, then said: Ride, O Uqbah. I said: Glory be to Allah, upon your mount? He commanded me and said: Ride. I said the like of that again and repeated it times until I feared I would disobey the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I rode his mount. Then he urged his she-camel and it stood. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me in a mountain pass and said: O Uqbah, shall I not teach you two surahs of the Qur'an, the best of the Qur'an or among the best? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He taught me the two protectors. Then he said: O Uqbah, when you see the dawn, inform me. When I saw the dawn I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the dawn. He made his mount kneel, then performed ablution, then established the prayer, then took my hand and placed me at his right. He recited them in the dawn prayer, then turned to me and said: O Uqbah, recite them whenever you rise and sleep."
"16027","929 - Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Maryam narrated, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I came with twelve riders until we shaded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). My companions said: Tend our camels, and we will go and take from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when we return in the evening we will share with you what we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I did that for days, then I thought to myself: Perhaps I am cheated; my companions hear what I do not hear and learn what I do not learn from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I attended one day, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution completely, then stands for his prayer, will be of his sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"16028","Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 930 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, both saying: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: A grey mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he rode it. Uqbah took to leading it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite. He said: What shall I recite, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak. He said: You never stand praying with anything like it."
"16029","931 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Himmani narrated (H). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both saying: Abu Usamah narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the two protectors. Uqbah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us with them in the dawn prayer."
"16030","Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 932 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, and he disliked drinking hot water, and when he applied kohl he applied it an odd number of times, and when he cleansed with stones he cleansed an odd number of times."
"16031","933 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Ibn Hubayrah and al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times, and when he cleanses with stones, let him cleanse an odd number of times."
"16032","934 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he applied kohl applied it an odd number of times, and when he cleansed with stones cleansed an odd number of times."
"16033","Thabit ibn Yazid, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 935 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Hasan, from Thabit ibn Yazid, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women who seek divorce impudently and tear away are the hypocrites."
"16034","Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 936 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki' narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Allah and unstained by unlawful blood will enter Paradise."
"16035","937 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays a prayer understanding it until he completes it, will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"16036","Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Uqbah. 938 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi narrated, both saying: Ibn Wahb narrated, Asim ibn Hakim informed me, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Pray in the resting places of sheep, and do not pray in the kneeling places of camels or the sitting places of camels."
"16037","Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Azraq, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 939 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Azraq, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two jealousies, one of which Allah loves and the other Allah hates, and two prides, one of which Allah loves and the other Allah hates. Jealousy in shooting Allah Almighty loves, and jealousy in other than it Allah hates. And pride: when a man gives charity Allah loves it, and pride in arrogance Allah hates it. And he said: Three whose supplication is answered: the father, the traveler, and the wronged. And he said: Indeed Allah admits three into Paradise by a single arrow: its maker, its giver, and its shooter in the path of Allah."
"16038","940 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Ibn Abi Adi narrated, Hisham narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir who said: I was told that Abu Sallam said: Abd Allah ibn Zayd narrated to me, that Uqbah ibn Amir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16039","941 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Yahya who said: Abu Sallam narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Allah Almighty admits into Paradise by a single arrow its maker who seeks good in his making, and its shooter and its giver. And he said: Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is dearer to me than that you ride. Everything with which a man amuses himself is false except his training his horse and his shooting with his bow and his playing with his wife."
"16040","Khalid ibn Zayd al-Juhani, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 942 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated (H). And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh and Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated (H). And Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, both saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, all saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated, Abu Sallam narrated to me, Khalid ibn Zayd narrated to me, saying: I was a shooter, and Uqbah ibn Amir would pass by me and say: O Khalid, come out with us to shoot. One day I was late for him, and he said: O Khalid, come, I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me. I came to him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah Almighty admits three persons into Paradise: its maker who seeks good in his making, and its shooter, and its supplier of arrows. Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is dearer to me than that you ride. There is no amusement except three: a man's training his horse, and his playing with his wife, and his shooting with his bow. Whoever abandons shooting after learning it, disliking it, it is a blessing he disbelieved in or abandoned."
"16041","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Uqbah. 943 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, al-Awza'i narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best with which those who seek refuge seek refuge: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind."
"16042","Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Hajabi, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 944 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Karabisi narrated, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Hajabi narrated, my father narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and tending was upon me and a companion of mine. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alone with people gathered around him, so I said to my companion: Suffice me until I sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and hear from him. I came to him and heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, and prays two rak'ahs turning to them, undistracted by anything, will emerge from his sins as his mother bore him."
"16043","Ba'jah ibn Abd Allah ibn Badr al-Juhani, from Uqbah. 945 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dust narrated, Abu Isma'il al-Qannad narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated, Ba'jah ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided sacrificial animals among his Companions, and a young goat fell to my lot. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a young goat fell to my lot. He said: Sacrifice it."
"16044","946 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ba'jah ibn Abd Allah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the sacrifices among his Companions, and a young goat fell to me, and he said: Sacrifice it."
"16045","947 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated (H). And Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Ba'jah ibn Abd Allah al-Juhani narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided sacrifices among his Companions. Uqbah said: A young goat fell to my lot, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, a young goat fell to my lot. He said: Sacrifice it. Al-Zuhri, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani."
"16046","948 - Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ubulli narrated, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Uqbah ibn Amir Abu Abis al-Juhani: I was with the Messenger of Allah in an army, and I pastured the mounts of my companions. When I returned to him in the evening, my companions came hastening, saying: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the caller called: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and he mentioned the like of the hadith."
"16047","Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 949 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both saying: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to me: Say, O Uqbah. I said to him: What shall I say? Then he was silent from me. I said to myself: If he repeats it to me I will say as he said. He said to me: Say. He recited: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, until he finished it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No asker asked nor any seeker of refuge sought refuge with the like of it."
"16048","950 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between al-Juhfah and al-Abwa', a wind and darkness covered us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began seeking refuge with: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and saying: O Uqbah, seek refuge, for no seeker of refuge sought refuge with the like of them. He said: Then I heard him leading us with them in prayer."
"16049","Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 951 - Al-Abbas ibn Ahmad al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated, Umayr ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Hanafi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to me, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You will never recite a surah dearer to me nor more effective than: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, so if you can never leave it in a prayer, then do so."
"16050","Abd Allah ibn Khubayb al-Juhani, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 952 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Sulayman, from Mu'adh ibn Abd Allah ibn Khubayb, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that he said: While I was leading the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an expedition, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say, O Uqbah. I said: What shall I say? He said it a third time. I said: What shall I say? He said: Say: He is Allah, the One. He recited the surah until he completed it, then he recited: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and I recited with him until he completed it. Then he recited: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and I recited with him until he completed it. Then he said: None sought refuge with the like of them."
"16051","Mu'adh ibn Abd Allah ibn Khubayb, from Uqbah. 953 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Mu'adh ibn Abd Allah who narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) young sheep."
"16052","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Uqbah. 954 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both saying: Waki' narrated, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Mu'adh ibn Abd Allah ibn Habib, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the young sheep, and he said: Sacrifice it."
"16053","955 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Mus'ab narrated, Attaf ibn Khalid narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be rulers who lead you in prayer; if they complete its bowing and prostration it is for you and for them, and if they fall short in it, it is for you and upon them."
"16054","Abd Allah ibn Ata', from Uqbah. 956 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Ata', from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we took turns tending. When my turn came I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people, and I heard him saying: No Muslim performs ablution and glorifies Allah, then stands in his prayer and knows what he says in it, but he turns accepted as on the day his mother bore him of sins, with no sin upon him. I could not restrain myself at that but said: Excellent, excellent."
"16055","Ma'bad ibn Hilal al-Abdi, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 957 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Ma'bad ibn Hilal, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Uqbah: Recite them in your prayer when you pray, for you never recite the like of them - meaning the two protectors."
"16056","Al-Hasan al-Basri, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 958 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made for us a warranty of slaves of three days."
"16057","959 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry, she belongs to the first."
"16058","960 - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Any woman married by two guardians belongs to the first of them."
"16059","961 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16060","Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Uqbah. 962 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Allaf narrated, Hilal ibn Hiqq narrated, from Ibn Awn and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: Uqbah ibn Amir went out to Maslamah ibn Mukhallad while he was governor over Egypt, and there was something between him and the deputies. When he came he entered upon him, and he said: Welcome to my brother, you came to me visiting. He said: I did not come to you visiting, but a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); you were with me that day. He said: Whoever knows an evil of his brother and conceals it for him, Allah will conceal for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"16061","Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Uqbah. 963 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verses were sent down to me the like of which I never heard, or: the like of which I never saw - the two protectors."
"16062","964 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya narrated, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verses were sent down to me the like of which was never sent down to me: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak."
"16063","965 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16064","966 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki' narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verses were sent down to me the like of which I never saw - meaning the two protectors."
"16065","967 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16066","968 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, from Bayan, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tonight verses were sent down to me the like of which was never seen at all: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind."
"16067","Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh, from Uqbah ibn Amir. 969 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki' narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Him and unstained by unlawful blood will enter Paradise."
"16068","Uqbah ibn al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal ibn Abd Manaf, his mother Khuzay'iyyah, his kunyah Abu Sirwa'ah. What Uqbah transmitted. 970 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, that Uqbah ibn al-Harith ibn Amir informed him, or he heard it from him - if he did not specify it - that he married Umm Yahya bint Abi Ihab, and a black slave woman said to him: I suckled you both. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it to him, and he turned away. I came to him a second time and mentioned that to him, and he said: How, when she claimed that she suckled you both? And he forbade him."
"16069","971 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah al-Bakrawi narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: Uqbah ibn al-Harith ibn Amir narrated to me, that he married Umm Yahya bint Abi Ihab, and a black slave woman came and said: I suckled you both. He said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he turned away from me. I mentioned that to him, and he said: How, when she claimed that she suckled you both? And he forbade him from her."
"16070","972 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, both saying: Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, that he married a woman, and a black slave woman came and claimed that she suckled them both. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned away from him. Then he mentioned a second time and said: She is lying. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: How, when it was said?"
"16071","973 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn, Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated, Uqbah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, saying: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab al-Taymi, and on the morning of her possession a freedwoman of my family in Mecca came and said: I suckled you both. I rode to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Medina and mentioned that to him, and said: I asked the girl's family and they denied. He said: How, when it was said? He said: I separated from her and married another."
"16072","974 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated (H). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: I heard Uqbah ibn al-Harith - and a companion of mine narrated to me, and I remember my companion's hadith - saying: I married Umm Yahya bint Abi Ihab, and a black woman came to us and claimed that she suckled them both together. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned away from me. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned away from me. I mentioned that to him, and he turned away from me. I said: She is lying. He said: How do you know that she is lying? She said what she said; leave her from you."
"16073","975 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Ayyub informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith - Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: And one more trustworthy than me narrated to me - that Umm Yahya was under him, and a black woman came and said: I suckled you both. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a black woman claimed that she suckled me and my wife, and she is lying. He turned away from him, then he repeated to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then leave her."
"16074","976 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah and Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, and a black woman came claiming that she suckled us. He turned away from me, so I came to him from the other side and he turned away from me. I faced him and said: O Messenger of Allah, she is black, and I began belittling her affair. He said: How, when it was said?"
"16075","977 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated (H). And Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, both saying: Wahb narrated, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith who said: Al-Nu'ayman or Ibn al-Nu'ayman was brought drunk, and it grieved the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) severely. He ordered those in the house to beat him, and they beat him with sandals and palm stalks. Uqbah said: I was among those who beat him."
"16076","978 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith who said: Al-Nu'ayman or Ibn al-Nu'ayman was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those in the house to beat him. I was among those who beat him, and we beat him with sandals and palm stalks."
"16077","979 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated, Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith who said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the afternoon prayer in Medina, and he gave the salam, then stood quickly stepping over people's necks to one of his wives' rooms. The people were startled by his haste, and he came out to them and saw that they were surprised at his haste, and said: I remembered some gold ore with me, and I disliked that it detain me, so I ordered its distribution."
"16078","Uqbah ibn Malik al-Laythi. 980 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated (H). And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated (H). And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated (H). And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated (H). And al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, all saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal who said: Abu al-Aliyah came to me, I and a companion of mine, and said: Come, for you two are younger than me and more retentive of hadith than me. He took us until he brought us to Bishr ibn Asim al-Laythi and said: Narrate your hadith to these two. Bishr said: Uqbah ibn Malik - of his tribe - narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment which raided a people. A man of the people broke away, and a man of the detachment followed him with his sword drawn. The stray man of the people said: I am a Muslim, but he did not consider what he said. He struck him and killed him. The report reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said severe words about it. It reached the killer. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching, the killer said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he said what he said only seeking refuge from killing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him of the people, and continued his sermon. Then he said a second time: By Allah, he said what he said only seeking refuge from killing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him of the people and continued his sermon. Then he could not refrain but said a third time: By Allah, he said what he said only seeking refuge from killing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him with displeasure known in his face, then said: Indeed Allah refused me regarding one who kills a believer - he said it three times."
"16079","981 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal who said: A man brought me together with Bishr ibn Asim, and he narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Malik, that an army of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon people at a watering place in the morning. A man from the water rose, and a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) charged at him. He said: I am a Muslim, but he killed him. When they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he was informed of that, and he stood preaching. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, what is the matter with a Muslim killing a Muslim while he says: I am a Muslim? He said: O Messenger of Allah, he said it seeking refuge. He said: Thus, and he turned his face away from him. He said: Indeed Allah refused me regarding one who kills a Muslim - he said it three times."
"16080","982 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Humaydah bint Ubadah al-Ansariyyah, from her sister, from Uqbah ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and preached upon the pulpit in Ramadan and said: I stood upon this pulpit knowing Laylat al-Qadr, so seek it in the last ten, in the odd night."
"16081","Uqbah Abu Abd al-Rahman. 983 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated, Nafi' ibn Sayfi narrated - and he had reached one hundred and twelve years - from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqbah, from his father Uqbah - and an arrow had struck him with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim who saw me will enter the Fire, nor one who saw one who saw me, nor one who saw one who saw one who saw me - three times."
"16082","Those named Iyad. Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, he resided in Basra. His lineage. 984 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated, from Abu Ubaydah Ma'mar ibn al-Muthanna who said: Iyad ibn Himar ibn Arfajah ibn Najiyah ibn Sufyan ibn Mujashi'."
"16083","985 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, from Abu al-Ala', from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Iyad ibn Himar, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lost property. He said: Announce it, and do not conceal nor hide it; if its owner comes, otherwise it is Allah's wealth which He gives to whom He wills."
"16084","986 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated (H). And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, both saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds a stray, let him call two just witnesses and not conceal; if he does not find its owner, it is Allah's wealth which He gives to whom He wills."
"16085","987 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of, of what He taught me this day of mine. He said: All wealth I granted My servants is lawful for them. I created My servants all upright, then devils came to them and diverted them from their religion, and forbade them what I made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me what I sent no authority for. Allah looked at the people of the earth and detested them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. Allah commanded me to fight Quraysh, and I said: O Lord, they will then crush my head until they leave it like bread. He said: I sent you only to test you and to test by you. I sent down to you a Book which water does not wash; you recite it in sleep and wakefulness. Fight them, Allah will honor you. Spend, it will be spent upon you. Send an army, We will reinforce you with five times their like. Fight with those who obey you those who disobey you. The people of Paradise are three: a just ruler, and a merciful man tender of heart to every kin and Muslim, and a rich, chaste, charitable man. And the people of the Fire are five: the weak with no resolve, those among you who are followers seeking thereby neither family nor wealth; a man who morning and evening deceives you about your family and wealth; a man whose greed is not hidden, even if small, but he goes for it; and the foul-mouthed obscene. He said: And he mentioned miserliness and lying..."
"16086","989 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated (H). And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, both saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds a stray, let him call two just witnesses and not conceal; if he does not find its owner, it is Allah's wealth which He gives to whom He wills."
"16087","990 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever comes upon lost property, let him call a just one to witness, then not conceal nor hide it, and announce it for a year; if its owner comes, otherwise it is Allah's wealth which He gives to whom He wills."
"16088","991 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Ala', from Iyad ibn Himar who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lost property, and he said: Announce it; if you find its owner, otherwise it is Allah's wealth which He gives to whom He wills. Ayyub did not mention Mutarrif in his hadith."
"16089","992 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, Abu Khalifah, and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, all saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, al-Ala' ibn Ziyad narrated to me, and Yazid, brother of Mutarrif, narrated to me, and two other men whose names Hammam forgot, that Mutarrif narrated to him that Iyad ibn Himar narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in his sermon: Indeed Allah Almighty commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of, of what He taught me this day of mine. All wealth I granted My servant is lawful. I created My servants all upright, and devils beset them and diverted them from their religion, and forbade them what I made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me what I sent no authority for. Allah Almighty looked at the people of the earth and detested them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. He said: O Muhammad, I sent you to test you and to test by you. I sent down to you a Book which water does not wash; you recite it awake and asleep. Allah revealed to me to fight Quraysh, and I said: O Lord, then they will crush my head and leave it like bread. He said: Drive them out as they drove you out, and fight them, We will honor you. Spend, it will be spent upon you. Send an army, We will send five times their like. Fight with those who obey you those who disobey you. He said: And he said: The companions of Paradise are three: a just, guided ruler, and a merciful man tender of heart to every kin and Muslim, and a chaste, poor, charitable man. And he said: The companions of the Fire are five: a man whose greed is not hidden, even a speck, but he takes its side; a man who evening and morning deceives you about your family and wealth; the weak with no resolve, those among you who are followers seeking neither family nor wealth - a man said: O Abu Abd Allah, are they of the freedmen or of the Arabs? He said: He is the follower belonging to a man, who violates his sanctity by fornication without marriage - and the foul-mouthed obscene. He said: And he mentioned lying and miserliness, and the wording is Abu Muslim's."
"16090","993 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, Qatadah narrated to me, al-Ala' ibn Ziyad narrated to me, and Yazid ibn Abd Allah, brother of Mutarrif, and Uqbah and another man, that Mutarrif narrated to them, from Iyad ibn Himar, that he attended the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard him saying: Indeed Allah Almighty commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16091","994 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"16092","995 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ala' Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He preached, and said in his sermon: Indeed Allah commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of, of what He taught me in this day of mine. All wealth I granted My servants is lawful. I created My servants all upright, and devils came to them and diverted them from their religion, and forbade them what I made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me what I sent no authority for. Then Allah Almighty looked at the people of the earth and detested them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. He said: I sent you only to test you and to test by you. I sent down to you a Book which water does not wash; you recite it asleep and awake. Allah commanded me to come to Quraysh, and I said: O Lord, then they will crush my head and leave it like bread. He said: Drive them out as they drove you out, and fight them, We will fight with you. Spend, it will be spent upon you. Send an army, I will send with it five like it. And he mentioned the hadith."
"16093","996 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Awf narrated (H). And Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Awf (H). Aslam said: And Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Awf (H). And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, Awf ibn Abi Jamilah narrated, from Hakim al-Athram, that al-Hasan narrated to them, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, Iyad ibn Himar narrated, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in a sermon he preached: Indeed Allah Almighty commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of, of what He taught me this day of mine. Verily all wealth I granted My servants is lawful for them. I created My servants all upright, and devils came to them and diverted them from their religion, and forbade them what I made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me what I sent no authority for. Allah looked at the people of the earth before He sent me and detested them all, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. Allah said: I sent you only to test you and to test by you. I sent down to you a Book which water does not wash; you recite it asleep and awake. Allah revealed to me to fight Quraysh, and I said: O Lord, then they will crush my head and leave it like bread. He said: Drive them out as they drove you out, and fight them, We will fight with you. Send an army, We will send five times their like. Spend, it will be spent upon you. Fight with those who obey you those who disobey you. He said: The people of Paradise are three: a just ruler, and a merciful man tender of heart to every kin and Muslim, and a rich, chaste, charitable man. And the people of the Fire are five: the weak with no resolve, and those among you who are followers seeking neither family nor wealth; a man who morning deceives you about your family and wealth; a man whose greed is not hidden, even if small, but he goes for it; and the foul-mouthed obscene. And he mentioned miserliness and lying."
"16094","997 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh al-Azdi, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Shall I not tell you what Allah Almighty told me in the Book: Indeed Allah Almighty created Adam and his sons upright Muslims. He gave them wealth lawful with no unlawfulness in it, yet they worshipped idols. He commanded me to come to them and make clear to them what He fashioned them upon. I addressed my Lord: If I come to them, Quraysh will crush my head as bread is crushed. He said to me: Proceed, I will proceed with you. Spend, it will be spent upon you. Fight those who disobey you with those who obey you, for I will give with every army you send ten times their like of angels, and I breathe terror into the chests of your enemy. We will give you a Book which water does not erase; I remind you of it asleep and awake. So mark me and Quraysh, and this Quraysh, for they bloodied my face and robbed me of my family, and I confront them. If I overcome them, they will come to what I called them to, willingly or unwillingly. If they overcome me, I was upon something I call you to."
"16095","998 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan, that Iyad ibn Himar came with a she-camel and a mount to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gifted them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lead it. He led it, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him: O Iyad ibn Himar, have you embraced Islam? He said: No. He said: Take your she-camel, for Allah forbade for us the froth of the polytheists."
"16096","999 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi, both said: Amr ibn Marzuq told us, Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Yazid, brother of Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, who said: I gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a she-camel or a sacrificial camel, and he said: Have you become Muslim? I said: No. He said: I have been forbidden from accepting the gifts of the polytheists."
"16097","1000 - Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ali ibn Said al-Razi, they said: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi told us, al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Shaybani told us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Matar al-Warraq, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his sermon: Allah Almighty revealed to me that you should be humble, so that no one boasts over another and no one wrongs another."
"16098","1001 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna: Musaddad told us, Yahya ibn Said told us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of my people insults me, is there any harm if I retaliate against him? He said: Two people who insult each other are two devils who vilify and lie against each other."
"16099","1002 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi told us, Hammam told us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two people who insult each other are two devils who lie against each other and vilify each other."
"16100","1003 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi: Amr ibn Marzuq told us, Imran ibn al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever two people who insult each other say, its sin is upon the one who started, unless the wronged one transgresses."
"16101","1004 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi told us, Hammam ibn Yahya told us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whatever two people who insult each other say is upon the one who started, so long as the wronged one does not transgress."
"16102","1006 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah died and appointed his cousin Iyad ibn Ghanm al-Fihri as his successor."
"16103","What Iyad ibn Ghanm transmitted 1007 - Narrated Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Zibriq al-Himsi: my father told us. And narrated Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri and Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi, they said: Ishaq ibn Zibriq al-Himsi told us, Amr ibn al-Harith told us, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, al-Fudayl ibn Fudalah told us, referring it to Ibn Aidh, and Ibn Aidh referring it to Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Iyad ibn Ghanm fell upon the owner of Dariyya when it was conquered, then Hisham ibn Hakim came to him and spoke harshly to him. Hisham stayed some nights, then came to him apologizing and said: O Iyad, did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people with the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who inflicted the severest punishment on people in this world? Iyad said to him: O Hisham, we have heard what you heard and seen what you saw and accompanied whom you accompanied. Have you not heard, O Hisham, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever has advice for one in authority should not speak to him about it openly, but should take him by the hand and be alone with him; if he accepts it, he accepts it, otherwise he has discharged his duty. And you, O Hisham, are indeed bold when you dare against the authority of Allah; why did you not fear that the authority of Allah might kill you, so you would be one killed by the authority of Allah."
"16104","1008 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari: Dahir ibn Nuh told us, Amr ibn al-Walid told us, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Yahya: Yahya ibn Jabir told us, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Iyad ibn Ghanm, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me one day: O Iyad, never marry an old woman nor a barren one, for I will boast of numbers through you over the nations."
"16105","1009 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi: Muhammad ibn Khalid told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Iyad ibn Ghanm, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he dies he enters the Fire, and if he repents Allah accepts it from him. If he drinks a second time, likewise; if he drinks a third time, likewise; if he drinks a fourth time, it becomes due upon Allah to give him to drink from the clay of al-Khabal. It was said: What is the clay of al-Khabal? He said: The excretions of the people of the Fire."
"16106","Iyad Abu Abdullah al-Thaqafi 1010 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad: Zayd ibn al-Harish and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim told us, they said: Abu Asim told us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala al-Taifi informed us, Abdullah ibn Iyad informed me, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Hawazin with twelve thousand, and on the day of Hunayn as many of our people of Taif were killed as were killed of Quraysh on the day of Badr. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a handful of gravel and threw it at our faces, and we were defeated."
"16107","1011 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari told us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad told us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala informed us, Abdullah ibn Iyad informed me, from his father, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a small skin of honey was gifted to him and he accepted it, and he said: Guard my mountain pass, so he guarded it for him, and he wrote a document for him."
"16108","Iyad al-Ansari 1012 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik told us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi told us, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Iyad al-Ansari, who was a Companion, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Preserve my honor regarding my Companions and my in-laws; whoever preserves my honor regarding them, Allah will preserve him in this world and the Hereafter, and whoever does not preserve my honor regarding them, Allah will disown him, and whoever Allah disowns, He is about to seize him."
"16109","Iyad ibn Zayd al-Abdi 1013 - Narrated Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Minqari told us, Uthman ibn Umar told us, from al-Nahhas ibn Qahm and Muhammad ibn Said, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, who said: A man of Abd al-Qays called Iyad told me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Hold fast to the remembrance of your Lord, and pray your prayers at the beginning of their time, for Allah Almighty will multiply reward for you."
"16110","Iyad ibn Marthad al-Amiri, and there is disagreement about his Companionship. 1014 - Narrated Abu Khalifah: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, Shubah told us, Asim ibn Kulayb informed me, he said: I heard Iyad ibn Marthad, or Marthad ibn Iyad al-Amiri, narrating to a man that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a deed that would admit him to Paradise, and he said: Is either of your parents alive? He said: No. He asked three times. He said: Give water to drink; carry it to them when they are away, and suffice them of it when they are present."
"16111","1015 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi told us, Shubah told us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said: I heard Iyad ibn Marthad, or Marthad ibn Iyad, from a man among them, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a deed that would admit him to Paradise, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16112","Iyad ibn Amr al-Ashari, who lived in Kufah 1016 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani: Sulayman ibn Harb told us. And narrated Abu Khalifah: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi told us, both said: Shubah told us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Iyad al-Ashari, who said: When this verse was revealed {Allah will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him} the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are the people of this one, meaning Abu Musa al-Ashari."
"16113","1017 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Ibn al-Asbahani told us. And narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, both said: Sharik told us, from Mughirah, from Amir, who said: Iyad al-Ashari attended an Eid at al-Anbar and said: Why is it I see them not chanting joyfully as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to chant."
"16114","Those named Ikrimah. Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl ibn Hisham ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum. His mother was Umm Mujalid, a woman of Banu Hilal. He became Muslim in the year of the Conquest, and was martyred on the day of Yarmuk in the caliphate of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both; and it is said he was martyred on the day of Ajnadayn. 1018 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari: Khalid ibn Khidash told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: When Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl swore a solemn oath he would say: By the One Who saved me on the day of Badr. And he would take the mushaf and place it on his face and say: The speech of my Lord, the speech of my Lord."
"16115","1019 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: When the day of the Conquest came, Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl fled and boarded the sea, and the sea became rough with them. The masts crew and those in the sea began calling upon Allah Almighty and seeking His help. He said: What is this? It was said: A place where nothing benefits except Allah. So Ikrimah said: Then this is the god of Muhammad to whom he calls us; take us back to him. So he returned and became Muslim, and his wife had become Muslim before him, and they remained upon their marriage."
"16116","1020 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: my father told me, Ibn Lahiah told us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, concerning the story of the Conquest, he said: Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl fled heading for Yemen. And Umm al-Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham came forward, being at that time a Muslim and being under Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl as his wife, and she sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to seek her husband, and he gave her permission and granted him safety. She set out with a Roman slave of hers, and he solicited her for himself; she kept holding out hope to him and drawing him near until she came upon some people of Akk and sought their help against him, and they detained him. She caught up with her husband at part of Tihamah, and he had boarded a ship; when he sat in it he called upon al-Lat and al-Uzza, so the crew of the ship said: No one may call upon anything here except Allah alone sincerely. So Ikrimah said: By Allah, if He alone is in the sea, He is alone on the land too. So he swore by Allah that he would return to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Ikrimah returned with his wife and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, and he accepted from him. And a man of Hudhayl entered upon his wife fleeing when Banu Bakr were defeated, and she blamed him and deemed him weak and reproached him for fleeing, and he said: [text breaks off here]."
"16117","1021 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Fahm: Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri told us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl ibn Hisham, and he left no offspring. He had gone out fleeing on the day of the Conquest until his wife sought permission for him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she being Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham, and he granted him safety. She caught up with him in Yemen and brought him back to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he stood up to him and embraced him and said: Welcome to the mounted emigrant."
"16118","What Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl transmitted 1022 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both said: Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan al-Thawri told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Musab ibn Sad, from Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day I came to him: Welcome to the mounted emigrant, welcome to the mounted emigrant. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave any expense I spent against you except that I will spend its like in the path of Allah."
"16119","Those named Alqamah. Alqamah ibn Rimthah al-Balawi 1 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi al-Misri: Abdullah ibn Salih told us. And narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi al-Misri: Yahya ibn Bukayr told us, both said: al-Layth ibn Sad told us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays al-Tujibi, from Zuhayr ibn Qays al-Balawi, from his uncle Alqamah ibn Rimthah al-Balawi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Amr ibn al-As to Bahrain, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out on a detachment, and we set out with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dozed off, then woke up and said: May Allah have mercy on Amr. So we discussed who was named Amr. Then he dozed a second time and woke up and said: May Allah have mercy on Amr. Then he dozed a third time and woke up and said: May Allah have mercy on Amr. We said: Which Amr, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Amr ibn al-As. They said: What about him? He said: I remembered him; whenever I called people to give charity he would bring charity generously, and I would say: Where did you get this from, O Amr? And he would say: From Allah. And Amr spoke the truth; indeed Amr has much good with Allah. Zuhayr said: When the tribulation occurred I said: I will follow this one, about whom the Messenger of Allah said what he said, so I never parted from him."
"16120","2 - Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud: Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar told us, Ibn Lahiah told us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays al-Tujibi, from Zuhayr ibn Qays al-Balawi, from Alqamah ibn Rimthah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Amr ibn al-As to Bahrain, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out and we set out with him, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Layth."
"16121","Alqamah ibn Faghwa al-Khuzai. 3 - Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti: Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Muawiyah ibn Hisham told us, from Shayban, from Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abdullah ibn Alqamah ibn Faghwa, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, we would speak to him and he would not speak to us, and we would greet him and he would not return our greeting until he came home and performed his ablution for prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we speak to you and you do not speak to us, and we greet you and you do not return our greeting? He said: Until the verse of concession was revealed {O you who believe, when you rise for prayer} the verse."
"16122","Alqamah ibn Najiyah ibn al-Harith Abu Kulthum al-Khuzai, then al-Mustaliqi. 4 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki: Yaqub ibn Humayd told us, Isa ibn al-Hadrami ibn Kulthum ibn Alqamah ibn Najiyah ibn al-Harith al-Khuzai told us, from his grandfather Kulthum, from his father Alqamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to us al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt to collect our wealth as charity. He traveled until he was near us, that being after the incident of al-Muraysi, then he turned back. So we mounted in his pursuit, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to a people in their ignorance who took up arms and withheld charity. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not react to that until there was revealed {O you who believe, if a corrupt person comes to you} the verse. And the Mustaliq came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) following al-Walid with a group of their charities driving them, and provisions they carried, and they mentioned that to him, and that they had gone out seeking al-Walid with their charities but did not find him. So they handed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what they had with them and said: O Messenger of Allah, we heard of the coming of your messenger and were glad of that, and we said: We will go out to meet him. Then we heard of his return, and we feared that was due to his displeasure with us. And they offered the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to buy from him what remained, so he accepted the obligatory dues from them and said: Return with your provisions; we do not sell anything of the charities until we take possession of it. So they returned to their families, and he sent to them one who would collect the rest of their charities."
"16123","5 - Narrated Ali ibn Ishaq al-Wazir al-Asbahani: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz al-Makki told us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Isa ibn al-Nadr ibn Kulthum ibn Alqamah al-Mustaliqi told us, my grandfather told me, from his father, that he was among the delegation of Banu al-Mustaliq to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the matter of al-Walid ibn Uqbah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Depart, neither detained nor besieged."
"16124","6 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki: Yaqub ibn Humayd told us, Isa ibn al-Hadrami ibn Kulthum ibn Alqamah ibn Najiyah ibn al-Harith al-Khuzai told us, from his grandfather Kulthum, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them in the year of al-Muraysi when they became Muslim: Part of the completeness of your Islam is that you pay the zakat of your wealth."
"16125","Alqamah ibn Nadlah. 7 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna: Musaddad told us. And narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, both said: Isa ibn Yunus told us, Umar ibn Abi Sad ibn Abi Husayn told us, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Alqamah ibn Nadlah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, as did Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, while the houses of Makkah were called only al-Sawaib: whoever was in need would reside, and whoever was self-sufficient would house others."
"16126","Alqamah ibn al-Huwayrith al-Ghifari. 8 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani: Shabab al-Usfuri told us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman told us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif told us, my grandfather told me, he said: I heard Alqamah ibn al-Huwayrith, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adultery of the two eyes is looking."
"16127","Alqamah ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, who used to live in Basrah. 9 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari: Said ibn Sulayman told us, Yunus ibn Bukayr told us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, Abd al-Karim al-Basri told us, Alqamah ibn Sufyan told me, he said: I was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he pitched for us a dome near the house of al-Mughirah. Bilal would bring us our breakfast in Ramadan while we were traveling at dawn, very early."
"16128","Alqamah ibn Ulathah al-Amiri. 10 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi: Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa told us, both said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, from Ibn Awn, that Alqamah ibn Ulathah came to Umar at night thinking he was Khalid ibn al-Walid when Umar had dismissed him, and he said: Do not be startled, may you lose your father; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek help through you, and he did not dismiss you. The hadith."
"16129","Alqamah Abu Awfa al-Aslami 11 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Abu Nuaym told us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim told us. And narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb told us. And narrated al-Husayn ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi: Affan ibn Muslim told us. And narrated al-Fadl ibn al-Hajjaj al-Jumahi: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi told us, they said: Shubah told us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: When people brought their charity to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: O Allah, bless them. So my father brought his charity, and he said: O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa."
"16130","Those named Adda. Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah al-Amiri, and he is: al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah ibn Khalid ibn Rabiah ibn Amr ibn Amir ibn Sasaah ibn Muawiyah ibn Bukayr ibn Hawazin ibn Mansur ibn Ikrimah ibn Hafsah ibn Qays ibn Ghaylan ibn Mudar ibn Nizar. 12 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jawhari narrated to me this lineage: Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Minqari told us, al-Asmai told us."
"16131","13 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: al-Minhal ibn Bahr told us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Yazid told us, he said: In the time of Yazid ibn al-Muhallab I set out to Makkah, I and Yahya ibn Abi Nasr. He said: We passed by a water called al-Tarjih. They said to us: Here is a man who saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we came to a very old shaykh. We said: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and he wrote for me concerning this water, and he brought out to us a skin containing the document of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: What is your name? He said: al-Adda ibn Khalid. We said: What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I was beneath his she-camel on the day of Arafah while it was chewing its cud, and he said: O people, what day is this? What month is this? What land is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Is this not a sacred month, a sacred land, and a sacred day? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Indeed your blood, your wealth and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet your Lord. O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, bear witness."
"16132","14 - Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati: Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari told us, al-Hunayd ibn al-Qasim told us, he said: I heard al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah say: We fought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah did not grant us victory nor make us prevail."
"16133","15 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zibaqi and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jawhari, both said: Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Muqri told us, al-Asmai told us, Uthman ibn al-Shahham told us, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, al-Asmai said: and he is Imran ibn Taym, a freedman of theirs, he said: al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah said: Shall I recite to you a document written for me by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We said: Yes. And in it was written: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is what al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah bought from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he bought from him a male slave or a female slave - Uthman doubted - a sale of a Muslim with no disease, no ghailah and no khibthah. Al-Asmai said: I asked Said ibn Abi Arubah about al-ghailah and he said: Running away, theft and adultery. And I asked him about al-khibthah; he said: Selling people under the covenant of the Muslims."
"16134","16 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi Abu Abdullah al-Qadi al-Ramahurmuzi: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzuq told me, Fahd ibn al-Bakhtari ibn Shuayb ibn Umar al-Azraq told us, Shuayb ibn Umar told me, he said: I set out to Makkah, and when I reached al-Dariyyah one of my brothers said to me: Would you like to meet a man who has Companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. He said: The owner of the dome pitched at such-and-such place. So I said to my companions: Come with us to him. So we rose, and when we reached the owner of the dome we greeted and he returned the greeting and said: Who are the people? We said: People of Basrah; it reached us that you have Companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat beneath his pulpit on the day of the Farewell Hajj. He ascended the pulpit and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Allah Almighty says: {O people, We created you from male and female and made you peoples and tribes that you may know one another; indeed the noblest of you with Allah is the most God-fearing}. So no Arab has superiority over a non-Arab, nor a non-Arab over an Arab, nor a black over a white nor a white over a black, except by God-consciousness. O company of Quraysh, do not come to me with this world carried upon your necks while people come with the Hereafter, for I will not avail you anything with Allah. We said: What shall we call you, what is your name? He said: I am al-Adda ibn Amr ibn Amir, the knight of al-Dahya in the pre-Islamic period."
"16135","17 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi: Muhammad ibn Marzuq told us, Fahd ibn al-Bakhtari ibn Shuayb told us, my grandfather told me, Shuayb ibn Amr told me, he said: I heard al-Adda ibn Khalid say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will not come until a man greets only whom he knows, and until mosques are taken as thoroughfares, and until a woman trades along with her husband, and until women and horses become cheap and will not become expensive until the Day of Resurrection."
"16136","18 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzuq told us, Salih ibn Umar ibn Shuayb told us, from his grandfather Shuayb ibn Amr, who said: We performed Hajj and passed by the road of al-Munkadir, which people used to take, and we lost the way. While we were like that, a Bedouin appeared before us as if springing from the earth and said to me: O shaykh, do you know where you are? I said: No. He said: You are at al-Dhawaib, and this white hill you see is the bones of Bakr ibn Wail and Taghlib, and this is the grave of Kulayb, brother of Muhalhil. Then he said to me: Would you like to meet a man with Companionship with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Companionship from whom you may hear? I said: Yes. So he took me to the dome of Adam, and there I saw a man whose eyebrows were bound with a band. I said: Who is this? He said: al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Amr ibn Amir, the knight of al-Dahiyah in the pre-Islamic period. So I said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he rose with a rising as if startled. Ibn Masud said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you rose as if startled. He said: Beware of the three impostor Dajjals. Ibn Masud said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, you have told us about the one-eyed Dajjal and about the most lying of liars, so who is the third Dajjal? He said: A man who emerges among a people, the first of them destroyed and the last of them cut off; upon them is a lasting curse, in a tribulation called al-Hariqah. And he is the bald Dajjal who devours the servants of Allah."
"16137","19 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki: Qays ibn Hafs al-Darimi told us, Sulayman ibn al-Harith told us, Jahdam ibn al-Dahhak told us, he said: I passed by al-Narjij and saw there an old man. They said: This is al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Describe him to me. He said: He had a handsome sabalah, and the Arabs used to call the beard al-sabalah."
"16138","20 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki: Qays ibn Hafs al-Darimi told us, Sulaym ibn al-Harith told us, Jahdam ibn al-Dahhak told us, from al-Adda ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah, who said: He brought out to us a document and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote it for me, his grant to me of this water in which I am."
"16139","Those named al-As. al-As ibn Hisham Abu Khalid al-Makhzumi, grandfather of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, among the residents of Makkah. 21 - Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal: Shayban ibn Farrukh told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from his father or his uncle, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), during the campaign of Tabuk, said: If plague falls in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if you are outside it, do not come to it."
"16140","Those named Utarid. Utarid ibn Hajib 22 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Muadh, from Utarid ibn Hajib, that he gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a garment of silk brocade which Kisra had given him as clothing. His companions came in and said: Has something been sent down to you from the sky? He said: What do you marvel at? A handkerchief of the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise is better than this. Then he said: O boy, go with it to Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah, and tell him to send me the khamisah."
"16141","Those named Aidh. Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani, brother of Rafi ibn Amr. Reports of Aidh ibn Amr 23 - Narrated Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj: Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Abbadani told us, Salih al-Murri told us, Khalid ibn Ayyub told us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Aidh ibn Amr, who was among those who pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beneath the tree, and he said: His wife gave birth and saw purity after twenty days, so she washed, then came to enter with him into his cover. He felt her touch and said: Who is this? She said: So-and-so. He said: What is the matter with you? She said: I saw purity and washed. So he struck her with his foot and removed her from his bed and said: Do not tempt me away from my religion until forty days have passed."
"16142","24 - Narrated al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi: Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari told us, Hashraj ibn Abdullah ibn Hashraj al-Murri told us, my father told us, from his father, from his grandfather Aidh ibn Amr: that he used to ride ornamented saddles and wear khazz, seeing no harm in that."
"16143","25 - Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi told me, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Thabit al-Bunani told us, that Aidh ibn Amr bequeathed that Abu Barzah al-Aslami should pray over him. So Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad mounted to pray over him, and when he reached the palace of Hisham it was said to him: He bequeathed that Abu Barzah should pray over him, so he mounted his animal returning."
"16144","What Aidh ibn Amr transmitted. al-Hasan from Aidh 26 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi: Arim Abu al-Numan told us. And narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Abu Rabiah Fahd ibn Awf told us. And narrated Abu Khalifah: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khuzai told us. And narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad: Shayban ibn Farrukh told us, they said: Jarir ibn Hazim told us, al-Hasan told us, he said: Aidh ibn Amr entered upon Ziyad and did not greet him as commander. So Aidh said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the worst of shepherds is al-Hutamah; beware lest you be among them. Ziyad said to him: Sit, for you are but from the dregs of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Aidh said to him: And was there dregs among them? Dregs were only after them and among others than them."
"16145","27 - Narrated al-Qasim ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani: Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub al-Karmani told us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr told us, Shubah told us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Aidh ibn Amr said to Ziyad: It used to be said to us: The worst of shepherds is al-Hutamah, and beware lest you be among them. So Ziyad said to him: You are from the dregs of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16146","Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from Aidh 28 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Thabit, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Aidh ibn Amr, that Abu Sufyan passed by Salman, Suhayb and Bilal, and they said: The swords of Allah have not yet taken their due from the neck of this one. Abu Bakr said: Do you say this to the elder of Quraysh and its chief? Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what they said. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, perhaps you angered them; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you angered them you have angered your Lord. So he returned to them and said: My brothers, perhaps I angered you? They said: No, O Abu Bakr, may Allah forgive you."
"16147","Abu Shimr al-Dubai from Aidh ibn Amr 29 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna: Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, from Shubah, Abu Shamir al-Dubai told me, he said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-hantam, al-dubba, al-naqir and al-muzaffat."
"16148","29 / 2 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, Ghundar told us, from Shubah, from Abu Shimr al-Dubai, who said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16149","Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ahwal from Aidh ibn Amr 30 - Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi: Asim ibn Ali told us. And narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both said: Shayban ibn Farrukh told us, both said: Abu al-Ashhab told us, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever receives something of this provision without asking and without inner aspiration, let him widen his provision through it; and whoever is rich, let him direct it to one needier than him."
"16150","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sad al-Muzani from Aidh ibn Amr 31 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad: Zayd ibn al-Harish told us. And narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa told us. And narrated Buhlul ibn Ishaq: my father told us. And narrated al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi al-Basri: Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari told us, they said: Hashraj ibn Abdullah ibn Hashraj told us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sad, who said: We entered upon Aidh ibn Amr on the day of Ashura, and he said: Milk for them, O boy. So the boy rose to a milch camel and milked it and brought them. He said to the one on his right: Drink. He said: I am fasting. He said: May Allah accept from you and from us. Then he said to the second, and he said: I am fasting, and he said the like of that. Then he said to the third and he said the like of that. He said: Are all of you fasting? You are about to take this day as the station of Ramadan. We used to fast this day before Ramadan was obligated upon us; when Ramadan was obligated upon us, the fasting of Ramadan abrogated the fasting of this day. And this day is voluntary, not obligatory; whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break his fast. When the people heard that from him, they all broke their fast. And the wording is that of the hadith of Zayd ibn al-Harish."
"16151","32 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi: my father told me. And narrated Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, both said: Hashraj ibn Abdullah ibn Hashraj told us, my father told me, from his father, who said: Aidh ibn Amr said: I was struck by a shot while fighting before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, on my face. When blood flowed upon my face, beard and chest, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took with his hand and wiped the blood from my face and chest to my nipples, then supplicated for me. Hashraj said: Aidh would inform us of that during his life; when he died and we washed him, we looked at what he used to describe to us of the trace of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the extent he used to tell us, upon his chest, and there was a flowing white mark like the blaze of a horse."
"16152","33 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad: Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi told us: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini told us, Hashraj ibn Abdullah ibn Hashraj told us, my father told me, from his father, from Aidh ibn Amr, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign; when we returned heading for Madinah, the wife of a man martyred with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept. He said: Who is this weeping woman? They said: Fatimah bint Adi. He said: You are entrusted to Aidh ibn Amr. So he married her to his father and entrusted him with her."
"16153","An unnamed shaykh from Aidh ibn Amr. 34 - Narrated Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani told us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman told us, from his father, an old shaykh told me, from Aidh ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a small cup or a large cup with little water in it, so he performed ablution with it, then ordered that it be sprinkled upon them - or he said doused upon them. He said: The fortunate one among us was he whom it struck. He said: And I think it struck them all. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed with them the forenoon prayer."
"16154","Aidh ibn Said al-Jasri, of the Hayy of Anazah of Rabiah 35 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani: Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti told us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi told us, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Nadr, from Umm al-Banin bint Sharahil al-Abdiyyah, from Aidh ibn Said al-Jasri, who said: We came as a delegation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father be ransom for you, wipe my face and supplicate for me for blessing. So he wiped my face and supplicated for me for blessing. Umm al-Banin, his wife, said: I never saw him wake from sleep except his face was glistening as if oiled, though he would suffice with dates."
"16155","36 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Aban: Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti told us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi told us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr, from Umm al-Banin bint Sharahil, from Aidh ibn Said, who said: Sumayr ibn Zuhayr al-Jasri said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother Salamah ibn Zuhayr set out emigrating to Allah Almighty and His Messenger, and some shepherds of your camels of Banu Ghifar met him and killed him in the sacred month, though there was blood between us and them in the pre-Islamic period. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned them and asked them about that. They said: We found him driving your camels and wanted to take them, and he refused us, so we killed him. I do not know whether he made them swear or believed them, except that he asked him about the Islam of his brother and found no proof, so he paid blood-money for him for the sanctity of the sacred month: fifty camels. He said: Those camels remained in his household the best livestock and of greatest blessing."
"16156","Aidh ibn Qurt 37 - Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah told us, Muhammad ibn Himyar told us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Sakuni, who said: I heard Aidh ibn Qurt say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer without completing it, it is supplemented for him from his supererogatory prayers until it is complete."
"16157","Those named Ukashah. Ukashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi, a Badri; his lineage: Ukashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi. 38 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi told us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq told us, in naming those who witnessed Badr: Ukashah ibn Mihsan ibn Harthan ibn Kabir ibn Ghanm ibn Dudan ibn Asad ibn Khuzaymah, ally of Banu Abd Shams."
"16158","39 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl told us, from Husayn, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nations were shown to me, and prophets, one or two prophets, would pass with a group with them. The hadith."
"16159","40 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqqashi told us, Yazid ibn Zuray told us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah Zamah told me, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, who said: Ukashah ibn Mihsan left my presence with a group of Banu Asad wearing their shirts. When I prayed Maghrib they returned, their shirts upon their arms carrying them. I said: O Ukashah, yesterday you went out wearing shirts and returned with your shirts upon your arms? They said: O Umm Qays, this is a day in which concession was granted to us that when we stone the Jamrah we may exit ihram into what is lawful for a non-pilgrim except women; then when evening comes and we have not completed the rites, we become in ihram again as we were before stoning. So we left your presence wearing shirts, and when evening came and we had not completed, we returned with our shirts upon our arms as you saw."
"16160","Those named Itban. Itban ibn Malik al-Ansari, then al-Khazraji, a Badri 41 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: my father told us, Ibn Lahiah told us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then of Banu Salim ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj, then of Banu al-Ajlan ibn Zayd ibn Ghanim ibn Salim: Itban ibn Malik ibn Amr ibn Ajlan ibn Zayd ibn Ghanm ibn Salim ibn Awf ibn Amr ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj."
"16161","42 - Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi told us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh told us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then of Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj: Itban ibn Malik ibn Amr ibn Ajlan."
"16162","What Itban ibn Malik transmitted 43 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami: Shayban ibn Farrukh told us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah told us, Thabit al-Bunani told us, from Anas ibn Malik, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi told me, from Itban ibn Malik, who said: Something befell my eyesight, so I sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I would love for you to come to me and pray in my house so I may take it as a place of prayer. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me with whomever Allah willed of his Companions. He entered upon him praying in his house, while his Companions conversed among themselves mentioning the hypocrites, then they attributed the bulk and enormity of that to Malik ibn al-Dukhshum, wishing he had supplicated against him so he perished, wishing evil had befallen him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: He says that but it is not in his heart. He said: No one testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah and then enters the Fire or the Fire consumes him."
"16163","44 - Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib: Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami told us, Amir ibn Yasaf told us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, who said: When Itban ibn Malik was afflicted in his eyesight, he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I would love for you to come to me and pray in my house and supplicate for us for blessing. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with a group of his Companions and they entered upon him. They conversed among themselves and mentioned Malik ibn al-Dukhshum; some said: O Messenger of Allah, he is the cave of the hypocrites and their refuge. They spoke much about him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not pray? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, a prayer with no good in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been forbidden from killing those who pray. Twice."
"16164","45 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Arim Abu al-Numan told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, Ali ibn Zayd told us, he said: We were with Anas ibn Malik, and he said to his son Abu Bakr: Narrate to them the hadith of Itban ibn Malik al-Ansari. So Abu Bakr narrated to us, with Anas witnessing, and said: I set out with my father to Syria; when he returned from Syria, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari walked with us bidding us farewell until, when he was about to part from us, he said: Shall I not narrate to you the hadith of Itban ibn Malik? We said: Yes. He said: He told me that his eyesight left him in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you came to my house and designated for me a mosque in it and prayed in it, so I may take it as a mosque; my eyesight has gone and I have become too weak to go out to the mosque. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised him a day he would come to him. When that day came, his companions gathered for him and assembled in my house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and heard them discussing the harshest of the people of Madinah against the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the greatest in enmity toward him; they traced that to Malik ibn al-Dukhshum. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked them: What are they discussing? He said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he keeps company with ... He said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if he says it truthfully from his heart, the Fire will never consume him. Anas said to me: Preserve this hadith, for it is among the treasures of knowledge. When we came to Madinah we found Itban ibn Malik alive, so I said to my father: Would you like to ask Itban about the hadith Mahmud narrated to us from him? So we went and asked him about it, and he narrated it to us."
"16165","46 - Narrated Abdullah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi: Ahmad ibn Hafs told us, my father told me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman told us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Abu Bakr ibn Anas, from Mahmud, who said: Itban ibn Malik lost his eyesight in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot pray with you in your mosque, and I would love for you to pray with me in my mosque so I may follow your prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, and they mentioned Malik ibn al-Dukhshum and said: He is the cave of the hypocrites and the refuge they take shelter in and their fortress. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes, but there is no good in his testimony. He said: No servant testifies to it truthfully from his heart and then dies except Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"16166","47 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi told me, from Itban ibn Malik, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My eyesight has failed me, and torrents come between me and the mosque of my people, and I would love for you to come and pray in my house at a spot I may take as a mosque. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will do so, if Allah wills. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abu Bakr and took him along; he set out with him and sought permission and entered. He said while standing: Where do you want me to pray? So I pointed to him where I wanted. He said: Then we detained him for a khazirah we had made for him. The people of the valley - meaning the people of the house - heard of him and flocked to him until the house was full. A man said: Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhshun or Ibn al-Dukhaysh? A man said: That is a hypocrite man who does not love Allah nor His Messenger. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: Do not say that of him while he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, as for us, we see his face and his talk among the hypocrites. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: Do not say that of him while he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He will never come on the Day of Resurrection saying: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah, except Allah forbids him to the Fire. Mahmud said: I narrated this hadith to a group among whom was Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, and he said: I do not think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said what you said. So I vowed that if I returned to Itban ibn Malik I would ask him; so I returned to him and found him a very old shaykh whose eyesight had gone, and he was the imam of his people. I sat beside him and asked him about this hadith, and he narrated it to me as he narrated the first time. Mamar said: When al-Zuhri narrated this hadith he would say: Then obligations and matters were revealed afterwards, and we consider the matter ended with them; so whoever can avoid altering, let him not alter."
"16167","48 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki: al-Qanabi told us, Ibrahim ibn Sad told us, from Ibn Shihab, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, from Itban ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forbidden to the Fire is whoever says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah."
"16168","49 - Narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani: Ismail ibn Abi Uways told us, Malik told me, from Ibn Shihab, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, that Itban ibn Malik used to lead his people in prayer while blind, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, there is darkness and rain and flood, and I am a man blind of sight, so pray, O Messenger of Allah, in my house at a spot I may take as a place of prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and said: Where would you like me to pray with you? He pointed him to a corner of the house, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in it."
"16169","50 - Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri: Ahmad ibn Salih told us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari told him, that Itban ibn Malik, one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, told him, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyesight has failed me, and I lead my people in prayer; when there are rains, the valley between me and them flows, and I cannot come to their mosque to pray with them. I wish, O Messenger of Allah, that you would come to me and pray in a place of prayer I may take as a place of prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will do so, if Allah wills. Itban said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in the morning with Abu Bakr when the day had risen; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission and I gave him permission. He did not sit until he entered the house, then said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed to a corner of the house. He stood and said takbir; we stood behind him and he prayed two rakahs then gave salutation. And we detained him for a khazirah we had made. Men of the household around us attained us until a number of men gathered in the house. One of them said: Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhshun? Some said: He is a hypocrite who does not love Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do that; do you not see he has said: There is no god but Allah, intending thereby the Face of Allah? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: His face and his counsel are but toward the hypocrites. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden the Fire for whoever says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah Almighty. Ibn Shihab said: Then I asked al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, one of Banu Salim, about the hadith of Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, and he confirmed it."
"16170","51 - Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri: Ahmad ibn Salih told us, Anbasah ibn Khalid told us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari informed me, that Itban ibn Malik, one of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, said: He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned the like of it."
"16171","52 - Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati: Ismail ibn Abi Uways told us, my father told me, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari, Itban ibn Malik informed me, that he was the imam of his people and had witnessed Badr, and he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When my eyesight worsened, crossing the valley when it flows between me and the mosque of my people became hard for me. So he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday: Have you considered, O Messenger of Allah, if you came to me and prayed at a spot in my house I may take as a place of prayer? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I will do so. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in the morning on Saturday with Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. He entered and did not sit until he said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed to the corner I wanted, and he prayed in it in the forenoon. And we detained him for a khazirah being made for him."
"16172","53 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, al-Layth told me, from Uqayl. And narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri: Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli told us, Salamah ibn Rawh told us, from Uqayl, Muhammad ibn Muslim informed me, that Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari informed him, that Itban ibn Malik, one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyesight has failed me and I lead my people in prayer; when there are rains, the valley between me and them flows, and I cannot come to their mosque to pray with them. I wish, O Messenger of Allah, that you would pray in a place of prayer I may take as a place of prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will do so, if Allah wills. Itban said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in the morning with Abu Bakr and Umar when the day had risen; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission and I gave him permission. He did not sit until he entered the house. He said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed to a corner of the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said takbir; we stood and formed rows and prayed two rakahs. Then a number gathered in the house. A speaker said: Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhayshin? Some said: He is a hypocrite who does not love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say that; do you not see he has said: There is no god but Allah, intending thereby the Face of Allah? He said: Allah knows best; we see his face and his counsel toward the hypocrites. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden the Fire for whoever says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah. Muhammad said: Then I asked al-Husayn ibn Muhammad, one of Banu Salim among their chiefs, about the hadith of Mahmud, and he confirmed it."
"16173","54 - Narrated Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti: Safwan ibn Salih told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir, from al-Zuhri, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi told me - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while he was five years old, and he remembered a mouthful of water the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spurted in his face from a bucket hanging in their house - he said: I heard Itban ibn Malik narrate, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyesight has begun to weaken with rains when they come, and the flood of the valley between my dwelling and the mosque of my people comes between me and prayer. I wish, O Messenger of Allah, that you would come to me and pray in my house at a place of prayer I may take as a place of prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: He came to me in the morning of the next day, he and Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission and I gave him permission. He did not sit until he said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed to a corner of my house. He said takbir, and we formed rows behind him and he bowed two rakahs, then gave salutation."
"16174","55 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi: al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Muallim told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, al-Awzai told us, Ibn Shihab told me, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari, who said: I remember a mouthful of water the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spurted in my face from a bucket hanging in our house. Mahmud said: Itban ibn Malik told me, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my eyesight has worsened, and when rains intensify, the valley flows between me and prayer in the mosque of my people. Would you pray in my mosque at a spot I may take as a place of prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me in the morning with Abu Bakr. They sought permission and I gave them permission. He did not sit until he said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed him to a corner. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward, and we formed rows behind him and he prayed. And we detained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a khazirah we had made for him."
"16175","56 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi: Muhammad ibn Musaffa told us, Muhammad ibn Harb told us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari - who claimed he remembered the Messenger of Allah while five years old, and claimed he remembered a mouthful of water the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spurted in his face from a bucket hanging in their house. Mahmud said: I heard Itban ibn Malik, a man of his tribe who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrate that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My eyesight has weakened, and when rains come, the flood of the valley between my dwelling and the mosque of my people prevents me and comes between me and prayer. I wish you would come and pray in my house so I may take it as a place of prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in the morning of the next day, he and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission and was given permission. He said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed to a corner of my house. He stood and said takbir; we formed rows behind him and he bowed two rakahs then gave salutation."
"16176","Those named Abis. Abis al-Ghifari 57 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi and Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, both said: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Yahya ibn Ayyub told me, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Abis al-Ghifari, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was on a roof and saw people departing. He said: What is the matter with people? They said: They are departing due to plague. He said: O plague, take me; O plague, take me; O plague, take me. The son of his brother said to him: He wishes for death, though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish for death, for it cuts off deeds, and a man is not returned so he may seek amends? He said: I fear six things I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention: unjust judgment, taking blood lightly, the rule of fools, severing kinship, multitude of police, and a people putting forward a man neither most understanding of them nor best of them to sing to them with the Quran."
"16177","58 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: my father told us: Zuhayr told us, Layth told us, from Uthman, from Zad han, who said: I was with Abis al-Ghifari atop a roof terrace in Basrah, and he saw people loading to flee from plague. He said: O plague, take me to you; O plague, take me to you; O plague, take me to you. A cousin of his said: He had Companionship; why does he wish for death? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you should wish for death, for then his term would be cut off. His cousin said: He had Companionship; why does he wish for death? And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fear for his nation: sale of judgment, rule of fools, multitude of police, severing kinship, taking blood lightly, and a generation who take the Quran as flutes, putting forward a man before them neither most understanding of them, only putting him forward to sing to them with it as singing."
"16178","59 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid told us. And narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji: Mahmud ibn Zanbur told us, Fudayl ibn Iyad told us, both from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zad han, from Abis al-Ghifari, who said: We were with him atop a roof terrace of his, and some people passed loading. He said: Who are these? It was said: They flee from plague. He said: O plague, take me; O plague, take me; O plague, take me. A nephew of his said to him: Though he had Companionship, he wished for death, though I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you should wish for death, for death is the last deed of the believer; he will not return so amends may be sought from him? He said: O son of my brother, I hasten ahead of traits I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that will be in the end of time, which he feared for his nation: rule of fools, multitude of police, taking blood lightly, severing kinship, and a generation emerging who take the Quran as flutes, putting forward a man neither most understanding of them in religion nor most knowledgeable, though among them are more understanding and more knowledgeable than them; they put them forward to sing to them as singing."
"16179","60 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari: Bishr ibn Adam told us, Amr ibn Asim told us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman told us, from his father, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Zad han, who said: We were with Abis al-Ghifari atop a roof terrace, and he saw people loading. He said: What is the matter with these? It was said: They flee from plague. He said: O plague, take me to you. A cousin of his said, though he had Companionship: He wished for death, though I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): None of you should wish for death. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Hasten with deeds before six: rule of fools, multitude of police, sale of judgment, taking blood lightly, severing kinship, and a generation who take the Quran as flutes, putting forward one of them to sing to them though he is least understanding in jurisprudence."
"16180","61 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Ibn al-Asbahani told us, Sharik informed us, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zad han, from Ulaym al-Kindi, from Abis al-Ghifari, that he saw people departing. He said: What is wrong with them? They said: They flee from plague. He said: O plague, take me to you. A cousin of his said to him: Do you wish for death? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Wish for death upon six traits: upon the rule of fools, sale of judgment, taking blood lightly, multitude of police, severing kinship, and a generation who take the Quran as flutes, putting forward a man to sing to them though he is not most understanding of them. Sharik added Ulaym al-Kindi in the chain."
"16181","62 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar: Ali ibn Hashram told us, Isa ibn Yunus told us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Zad han, from Abis al-Ghifari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fear for his nation six traits: rule of children, multitude of police, bribery in judgment, severing kinship, taking blood lightly, and a generation who take the Quran as flutes, putting forward a man neither most understanding of them nor best of them to sing to them as singing."
"16182","63 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari: Abu Yusuf al-Farisi told us, Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban told us, Mindal told us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Zad han, from Abis al-Ghifari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"16183","Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who used to live in Damascus. al-Sha bi from Awf ibn Malik 64 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah told us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ibn Ashwa, from al-Sha bi, from Awf ibn Malik: that he saw a Christian driving a woman, and he prodded her so she fell and he exposed her. So I struck him with a stick I had and wounded him in the head. I went to Muadh ibn Jabal and said: Protect me from Umar, for I feared his hastiness. He came to Umar and informed him; he brought us together and kept at the Christian until he confessed. He ordered a stick for him and it was carved, then he said: These have a covenant, so fulfill their covenant so long as they fulfill for you; if they alter, they have no covenant. And he ordered him and he was crucified."
"16184","Abu Ayyub al-Ansari from Awf ibn Malik 65 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih al-Azdi told us, from Muhammad ibn Harb, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us at midday while alarmed, and said: Obey me so long as I am among you, and hold fast to the verses of Allah; declare lawful what He made lawful and declare unlawful what He made unlawful."
"16185","Abu Hurayrah from Awf ibn Malik 66 - Narrated Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri: Abu Umayyah al-Wasiti told us, Yazid ibn Harun told us, Yazid ibn Iyad informed us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick, and follow funeral processions."
"16186","Abu Muslim al-Khawlani, whose name is Abdullah ibn Thuwab, from Awf 67 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi, both said: Abu Mushir told us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Muslim al-Khawlani, the trustworthy beloved, the trustworthy - to me he is beloved, and to me he is trustworthy - Awf ibn Malik told me, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nine or eight or seven, and he said: Will you not pledge to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He repeated it three times. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we have already pledged to you; upon what shall we pledge to you? He said: That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, and the five prayers - and he concealed a hidden word - : that you ask people for nothing."
"16187","Abu Idris al-Khawlani from Awf 68 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Will you not pledge to me? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we pledged to you once; upon what shall we pledge to you? He said that three times. He said: You pledge to me that you associate nothing with Allah, establish prayer, give zakat, hear and obey. Then he followed that with a hidden word: and that you ask people for nothing."
"16188","69 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah told us. And narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz: Said ibn Mansur told us, both said: Hushaym told us, Dawud ibn Amr told us, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah al-Hadrami, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai told us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to wipe over the leather socks during the campaign of Tabuk, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"16189","70 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi: my father told me, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr told us, Zayd ibn Waqid told me, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, Abu Idris al-Khawlani told me, Awf ibn Malik told me, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a tent of leather. He performed a firm ablution and said: O Awf, count six before the Hour. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: My death. He said: I was struck with grief at it. He said: Say: One. I said: One. And the second: the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis. And the third: a pestilence among you like the nasal discharge of sheep. And the fourth: wealth flowing until a man is given a hundred dinars yet remains dissatisfied with it. Then a tribulation leaving no Arab house but entering it. And a truce between you and Banu al-Asfar, then they betray and come to you under eighty banners, each banner twelve thousand."
"16190","Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami from Awf ibn Malik 71 - Narrated Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi al-Qurashi: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Farqad told us, my father Abdullah ibn al-Ala told me, from Makhul, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a leather tent of his. I greeted him and said: May I enter? He said: Enter. So I put my head in, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was performing a firm ablution. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I enter wholly? He said: Wholly. When I sat he said to me: Count six traits before the Hour: the death of your Prophet. Awf said: I was struck with grief at that, a grief like I never felt. He said: Say: One. I said: One. He said: And the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, and a tribulation in which there is the pestilence of the Arabs, a disease that seizes you like the throat-disease of sheep. And wealth spreading among you until a man is given a hundred dinars yet remains dissatisfied. And a truce between you and Banu al-Asfar; they betray and come to you with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"16191","72 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti: Abu al-Yaman told us, Safwan ibn Amr told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a building of his. I greeted him, and he said: Awf ibn Malik? I said: Yes. He said: Enter. I said: All of me or part of me? He said: Rather all of you. He said to me: O Awf, count six before the Hour: the first of them my death. And I wept until he began to quiet me. Then he said to me: Say: One. He said: And the second: the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis. Say: Two. I said: Two. He said: And the third: a pestilence occurring in my nation seizing them like the throat-disease of sheep. Say: Three. I said: Three. He said: And the fourth: a tribulation occurring in my nation, and he magnified it. Then he said: Say: Four. I said: Four. He said: And the fifth: wealth flowing among you until a man is given a hundred dinars yet is dissatisfied with it. Say: Five. I said: Five. He said: And the sixth: a truce between you and Banu al-Asfar; they will march against you with eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand. The encampment of the Muslims on that day will be in a land called al-Ghutah, in a city called Damascus."
"16192","73 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: There is no sin but I know its repentance. It was said: What is its repentance? He said: That he leaves it then does not return to it."
"16193","74 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told me, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I hope the hour of Friday is in one of three hours: when the caller calls, when the imam ascends the pulpit, and at the iqamah."
"16194","75 - Narrated Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj: Yahya ibn Bukayr told us, al-Layth told me. And narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, al-Layth told me, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked to the sky one day and said: This is a time when knowledge will be taken away. A man of the Ansar called Ziyad ibn Labid said to him: O Messenger of Allah, will knowledge be taken away though it is firmly established and hearts have retained it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I considered you among the most understanding of the people of Madinah. Then he mentioned to him the misguidance of the Jews and Christians despite what they possess of the book of Allah. Then I met Shaddad ibn Aws and narrated to him the hadith of Awf, and he said: Awf spoke the truth; shall I not inform you of the first of that to be taken away? He said: Humility; you will see no humble one."
"16195","76 - Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisisi: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb informed us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu Hamzah ibn Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over a funeral, saying: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, pardon him, grant him health, honor his lodging, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow and hail, cleanse him of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt, settle him in a house better than his house, a family better than his family, and a spouse better than his spouse, and protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire. Awf ibn Malik said: I wished I were the deceased due to the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16196","77 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh: my father told us. And narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisisi: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq told us, both said: Isa ibn Yunus told us, Abu Hamzah al-Himsi told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over the funeral of a man of the Ansar, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16197","78 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a funeral, and I memorized of his supplication while he said: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him health, pardon him, honor his lodging, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow and hail, cleanse him of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt, replace for him a house better than his house, a family better than his family, and a spouse better than his spouse, admit him to Paradise, and protect him from the punishment of the grave and from the punishment of the Fire. Until I wished I were that deceased one."
"16198","79 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, Muawiyah ibn Salih told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of this hadith."
"16199","80 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi told us, Safwan ibn Amr told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: When fay came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would divide it the same day, giving the married two shares and the unmarried one share."
"16200","81 - Narrated Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi: al-Hakam ibn Nafi told us. And narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Yazid al-Hawti, both said: Abu al-Mughirah told us, both said: Safwan ibn Amr told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr told me, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: When fay came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would divide it the same day, giving the married two shares and the unmarried one share. We were called, and I was called before Ammar ibn Yasir, and I was given one share. He was displeased until the Messenger of Allah and those present recognized that. A remainder of gold was left, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began lifting it with the tip of his staff and it would fall, then he would lift it and it would fall, while saying: How will you be on the day this is hoarded for you? No one answered him. Ammar ibn Yasir said: By Allah, we wish it were hoarded for us; then whoever is patient would be patient, and whoever is tempted would be tempted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Perhaps you will be among its worst tempted."
